Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.77,0:02:49.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, ma'am,\Nhow ya doin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.47,0:02:51.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this Rose Hill?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.84,0:02:54.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Good,\NThis is Ed Couch.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.48,0:02:56.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Vesta Adcock's nephew.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.98,0:02:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to get up there\Nand see her,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.28,0:03:03.29,Default,,0,0,0,,but I'm gonna be late\N'cause I'm lost out here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.35,0:03:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We're off the Alabama interstate\Nbut I don't know where.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.26,0:03:46.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- Did you hear that?\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.23,0:03:48.30,Default,,0,0,0,,The train.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.36,0:03:51.24,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I didn't hear\Nno train.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.00,0:03:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, nothin',\NI guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.40,0:03:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where's "Whistle Stop"\Non the map?\N- I can't find it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.87,0:04:03.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did you tell me to\Nturn right 10 miles back there?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.28,0:04:08.82,Default,,0,0,0,,God, you got a negative\Nsense of direction, hon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.88,0:04:11.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.82,0:04:16.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Ed,your aunt's gonna be\Nso disappointed we're late.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.09,0:04:20.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I know she's\Nbeen looking forward to\Nthis visit all week long.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.16,0:04:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Bless her sweet,\Nlittle ol' heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.57,0:04:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, how's my sweet Auntie V\Nthis afternoon?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.50,0:04:33.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember us?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.17,0:04:36.24,Default,,0,0,0,,- Don't you look pretty!\N- We brought you something.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.31,0:04:39.48,Default,,0,0,0,,- Let me look at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.55,0:04:42.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you know\NEvelyn loves you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.22,0:04:47.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, honey,\NI guess it'd be better if\Nyou wait out here for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.12,0:04:51.59,Default,,0,0,0,,-I'll get all this stuff.\N- Well, if you think it's best.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.66,0:04:54.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I do this time.\NOkay?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.03,0:04:57.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Have a nice day,\NAunt Vesta.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.27,0:04:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you pitch a fit\Nlike that'
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.18,0:05:13.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you know\Nthey took my gallbladder out?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.32,0:05:17.46,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.52,0:05:21.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes. Still\Nin the hospital in ajar.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.26,0:05:26.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess that's where\Nthey keep 'em.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.13,0:05:28.11,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.16,0:05:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,When I was\Nin the hospital,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.46,0:05:34.43,Default,,0,0,0,,the nurse gave me one of them\NFleet enemas they're so fond of.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.50,0:05:37.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Cleo Threadgoode,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.17,0:05:40.48,Default,,0,0,0,,82 year old widow,\Nimagine that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.54,0:05:43.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually,\Neverybody calls me Ninny.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.74,0:05:45.98,Default,,0,0,0,,'Course I'm\Njust visitin' here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.05,0:05:51.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you ever have\None of them Fleet enemas?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.39,0:05:53.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Um,well?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.39,0:05:55.46,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.52,0:05:58.76,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd remember it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.83,0:06:02.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Me and my friend, Mrs. Otis,\Ncome from Whistle Stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.56,0:06:04.77,Default,,0,0,0,,You ever been\Nto Whistle Stop?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.83,0:06:08.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, yes. I just\Npassed by there today.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.30,0:06:13.18,Default,,0,0,0,,She's lived\Ndown the street from me\Nfor 30 years or more.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.24,0:06:15.24,Default,,0,0,0,,After her son died,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.31,0:06:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,her daughter-in-law had a fit\Nfor her to come live\Nat the nursing home.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.98,0:06:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,They asked me to come\Nand be her roommate.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.35,0:06:26.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Otis don't know it,\Nbut I'm going home just soon\Nas she gets settled in good.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.92,0:06:32.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Does the name\N"Idgie Threadgoode"\Nring a bell?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.39,0:06:35.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, no, ma'am.\NI don't think so.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.00,0:06:38.81,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd remember her.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.87,0:06:42.78,Default,,0,0,0,,You see,\NI was practically adopted\Nby the Threadgoode family.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.84,0:06:45.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- I married her brother, Cleo.\N- Oh, uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.24,0:06:50.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie and her friend Ruth,\Nran the Whistle Stop Cafe.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.08,0:06:52.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.08,0:06:54.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie was a character,\Nall right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.85,0:06:58.20,Default,,0,0,0,,But how anybody\Ncould've thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.25,0:07:02.29,Default,,0,0,0,,she murdered that man\Nis beyond me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.36,0:07:04.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.39,0:07:07.96,Default,,0,0,0,,You sit and relax a while.\NI'll tell you all about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.03,0:07:10.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, now, let's see.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.73,0:07:14.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I 'member the day they pulled\Nthat truck up out of the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.88,0:07:20.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie was Buddy's pet\Nfrom the day she was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.22,0:07:27.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I 'member the day we\Nwas all gettin' ready\Nfor Leona's weddin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.05,0:07:29.03,Default,,0,0,0,,The war had just ended,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.09,0:07:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,the Great one,\Nyou know.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.49,0:07:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And another one\Nwas about to begin in\Nthe Threadgoode house.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.23,0:07:38.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Sipsey hone )4\Nis that finished?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.23,0:07:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- Buddy,\Nget dressed honey.\N- Mama?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.24,0:07:45.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Leona, what is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.27,0:07:47.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie's upstairs\Nin her room...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.21,0:07:49.19,Default,,0,0,0,,and says she won't come out\Nas long as she lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.24,0:07:51.38,Default,,0,0,0,,- She is gonna ruin my weddin'!\N- Shh.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.44,0:07:54.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Leona, you're gonna be\Nthe most beautiful bride.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.31,0:07:57.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course she is, Papa.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.65,0:08:01.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Your papa has spent\Nevery last nickel he has\Njust to make you happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.65,0:08:05.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, you try to act\Na little grateful, young lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.53,0:08:08.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Imogene Louise Threadgoode!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.70,0:08:11.24,Default,,0,0,0,,This is your mama!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.63,0:08:18.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You come down here right now.\NDo you hear me?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.64,0:08:21.28,Default,,0,0,0,,- Buddy, fetch her.\NShe'll listen to you.\N- Come on down, little bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.34,0:08:23.91,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no firin'\Nsquad waitin' for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.98,0:08:29.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Ohh! Come on, honey\NLet us see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.38,0:08:31.55,Default,,0,0,0,,You look so pretty.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.62,0:08:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,- I see London,\NI see-\N- Hush!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.19,0:08:39.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Julian, hush.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.69,0:08:42.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Come ahead, sweetheart.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.50,0:08:46.24,Default,,0,0,0,,You look awful nice\Nin that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.30,0:08:47.90,Default,,0,0,0,,- Mama!\N- You look fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.97,0:08:50.47,Default,,0,0,0,,She looks like a monkey
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.54,0:08:52.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Julian, stop it\Nright this second!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.41,0:08:55.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Take it back!\NTake it back!\NIdgie, hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.81,0:08:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you she\Nwas gonna ruin my weddin'!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.98,0:09:01.36,Default,,0,0,0,,- Idgie, get up.\N- Take it back!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.41,0:09:03.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Take it back!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.65,0:09:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'll get you for this.\N- No, Buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.79,0:09:13.86,Default,,0,0,0,,We have to be careful\Nwhen she's dressing up.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.93,0:09:15.88,Default,,0,0,0,,She's just a pain!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.93,0:09:19.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Leona, will you\Nstop shrieking'
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.53,0:09:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,This is your\Nweddin ' day'
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.25,0:09:36.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I oaks like you got yourself\Nup a tree, little bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.15,0:09:39.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sick of people\Nmakin' fun of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.25,0:09:41.79,Default,,0,0,0,,So you're gonna stay up here\Nall day long.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.85,0:09:45.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Yep.\NThe hell with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.12,0:09:49.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Who wants to wear\Nthat stupid ol' dress anyway?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.13,0:09:52.51,Default,,0,0,0,,- I ever tell you about the oysters?\N- Oysters?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.57,0:09:54.52,Default,,0,0,0,,- I tell you about the oysters?\N- No.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.57,0:09:59.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Think about the millions of\Noysters lyin' around the ocean.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.31,0:10:01.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Then one day...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.71,0:10:04.52,Default,,0,0,0,,God comes along and sees one\Nand he says,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.58,0:10:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,"I think I'm gonna make\Nthat one different."
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.55,0:10:09.76,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what he does?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.82,0:10:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,He puts a little\Npiece of sand in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.05,0:10:17.29,Default,,0,0,0,,- Guess what it can do\Nthat the others can't.\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.36,0:10:20.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It can make\Na beautiful pearl.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.73,0:10:22.90,Default,,0,0,0,,What if God\Nmade a mistake?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.96,0:10:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, the way I figure it,\Nhe never makes mistakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.13,0:10:30.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, he made sure\Nwe got together.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.97,0:10:32.97,Default,,0,0,0,,He made sure you got\Nthe best looking,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.04,0:10:35.25,Default,,0,0,0,,most charmin' brother\Nin the world...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.31,0:10:38.69,Default,,0,0,0,,- who's gonna beat you\Nto the chocolate cake.\N- You will not.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.75,0:10:41.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Got you out of the tree,\Ndidn't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.18,0:10:44.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Did not!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.18,0:10:47.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Into this estate,\Nthese two come now to be joined
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.89,0:10:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,If any man present\Ncan show cause...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.06,0:10:52.47,Default,,0,0,0,,why they may not lawfully\Nbe joined together,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.53,0:10:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,let him speak now or\Nforever after hold his peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.73,0:11:00.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Please be seated.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.77,0:11:04.98,Default,,0,0,0,,If either of you\Nknow any reason...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.04,0:11:08.02,Default,,0,0,0,,why you may not justly\Nbe joined together\Nin holy matrimony
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.07,0:11:10.55,Default,,0,0,0,,do you now confess it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.19,0:11:22.90,Default,,0,0,0,,It is then your will\Nto proceed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.96,0:11:26.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you,\NCharles Osgood justice-
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.50,0:11:35.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you. I don't know what\Nwe'd do without your generosity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.90,0:11:38.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Sipsey, especially you.\NLook what you've clone!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.94,0:11:42.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Mrs. Threadgoode.\NGimme that, you rascal!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.21,0:11:49.78,Default,,0,0,0,,John!\NJump on my back
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.85,0:11:53.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think\Nthere ever was a sweeter boy\Nthan Buddy Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.55,0:11:58.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- You look beautiful, Lily.\N- Yes, Lily, you sure do.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.12,0:12:01.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I had the biggest crush\Non him.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.63,0:12:03.97,Default,,0,0,0,,He was a terrible flirt!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.03,0:12:07.27,Default,,0,0,0,,But his heart belonged\Nto Ruth Jamison.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.33,0:12:10.50,Default,,0,0,0,,She was the daughter of\Na friend of his mama's...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.57,0:12:13.38,Default,,0,0,0,,who was visitin'\Nthat summer.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.44,0:12:16.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth Jamison,\Nyou're just the one\NI've been lookin' for.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.98,0:12:20.09,Default,,0,0,0,,- Are you thirsty?\N- Let's go visit\Nsomeplace else.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.99,0:12:29.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Think that's a big lake,\Nyou should've seen the\None next to our house.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.39,0:12:31.53,Default,,0,0,0,,We used to swim in it\Nand fish.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.59,0:12:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I sure do miss it.\NSure do.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.33,0:12:37.07,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened to it?\NDid it dry up?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.13,0:12:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,No, worse than that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.13,0:12:41.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Last fall,\Na ﬂock of ducks,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.27,0:12:45.55,Default,,0,0,0,,40 or 50 of 'em,\Nlanded right smack\Nin the middle of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.61,0:12:47.49,Default,,0,0,0,,This ﬂuke thing\Nhappened.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.54,0:12:50.02,Default,,0,0,0,,The temperature dropped so fast\Nthat the whole lake froze...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.08,0:12:52.08,Default,,0,0,0,,in three seconds,\Njust like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.15,0:12:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Those poor little ducks.\NDid it kill them?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.51,0:12:57.72,Default,,0,0,0,,No, they ﬂew off\Nand took the lake with 'em.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.78,0:13:01.16,Default,,0,0,0,,To this very day, that lake\Nis somewhere over in Georgia.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.22,0:13:04.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.64,0:13:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Come a little closer.\NI wanna give you something.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.04,0:13:21.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Come here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.34,0:13:27.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoop!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.72,0:13:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Come back here, hat. Where\Ndo you think you're gain'?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.36,0:13:39.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.36,0:13:42.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I got it.\NHold on, Ruth.\NHold on, little bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.87,0:13:49.61,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right.\NI got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.74,0:13:55.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Come here,\Nyou damn hat.\NGot it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.54,0:13:58.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I meant\Nto do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.55,0:14:03.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I... got it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.35,0:14:05.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Ta-da!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.02,0:14:09.56,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.\NDamn!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.62,0:14:11.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.23,0:14:23.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on. Get out.\NGet out.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.17,0:14:25.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.17,0:14:28.41,Default,,0,0,0,,- Buddy!\N- Buddy Threadgoode!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.04,0:14:31.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.81,0:14:33.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.01,0:14:37.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out of there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.48,0:14:42.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.36,0:14:45.50,Default,,0,0,0,,- Come on, Buddy!\N- Buddy'
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.56,0:14:48.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.70,0:14:53.31,Default,,0,0,0,,No-o-o!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.37,0:14:57.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.27,0:15:00.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy, no!\NNo!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.74,0:15:03.52,Default,,0,0,0,,No! Buddy!\NNo-o-o!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.58,0:15:06.62,Default,,0,0,0,,No! Buddy!\NLet me go!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.08,0:15:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,' No!\N- Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.95,0:15:15.59,Default,,0,0,0,,- You got to go back to the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.66,0:15:18.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.\NWe're gonna go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.22,0:15:21.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- Buddy!\N- You have to be strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.13,0:15:24.04,Default,,0,0,0,,- It'll be okay.\N- Buddy!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.10,0:15:27.05,Default,,0,0,0,,"The Lord is my Shepherd,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.10,0:15:29.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I shall not want."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.37,0:15:32.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, it like\Nto have killed us all
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.44,0:15:35.11,Default,,0,0,0,,But nary a one took it\Nas hard as Idgie,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.21,0:15:43.68,Default,,0,0,0,,everyone thought she 'o' die\Nright along with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.33,0:16:04.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Night alter night,\Nshe stayed by the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.67,0:16:08.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Big George was the only soul\Nshe'd let near her,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.91,0:16:12.45,Default,,0,0,0,,and he watched over her\Nnight and day
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.51,0:16:15.32,Default,,0,0,0,,You know,\Na heart can be broken,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.38,0:16:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,but it still keeps a-beatin'\Njust the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.52,0:16:21.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Miss Idgie, you'll have\Nto keep this blanket on...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.22,0:16:24.13,Default,,0,0,0,,or you'll catch\Nyour death of cold,\Nyou hear me now?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.19,0:16:28.61,Default,,0,0,0,,That's so sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.00,0:16:36.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.67,0:16:38.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you like\None of these?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.74,0:16:40.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, thank ya,\Nhoney.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.81,0:16:42.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.74,0:16:44.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Honey,\Nwe gotta get goin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.98,0:16:47.39,Default,,0,0,0,,The Braves' game's\Nfixin' to start...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.45,0:16:49.09,Default,,0,0,0,,and you're gonna miss\Nyour... thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.15,0:16:52.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me.\NThat's my husband, Ed.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.95,0:16:55.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, ma'am.\NHow you doin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.09,0:16:58.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Um.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.59,0:17:00.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe\NBuddy died.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.73,0:17:03.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Neither could I.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.40,0:17:06.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, well, I enjoyed\Ntalkin' to you, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.87,0:17:08.87,Default,,0,0,0,,What's your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.93,0:17:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn...\NEvelyn Couch.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.07,0:17:16.85,Default,,0,0,0,,- I've got to go.\N- You come back and see me,\Nyou hear?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.91,0:17:20.82,Default,,0,0,0,,- Okay.\N- Bye-bye.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.01,0:17:23.29,Default,,0,0,0,,First of all,\NI want you...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.35,0:17:25.96,Default,,0,0,0,,to truly\Ndedicate yourselves...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.02,0:17:30.06,Default,,0,0,0,,to finding little ways\Nto putting that magic,\Nthat spark...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.12,0:17:32.33,Default,,0,0,0,,back into your marriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.39,0:17:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,When we think of\Nromance and marriage,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.40,0:17:40.44,Default,,0,0,0,,- what is the first thought\Nthat comes into your mind?\N- Divorce!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.50,0:17:44.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember when counselors\Nused to tell you to wrap\Nyourself in cellophane...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.27,0:17:46.48,Default,,0,0,0,,to put a little charge\Ninto your marriage?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.54,0:17:49.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Do we really pay\Nfor these lectures?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.41,0:17:52.12,Default,,0,0,0,,You can see,\Nit is truly up to you...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.18,0:17:55.68,Default,,0,0,0,,to put romance back\Ninto your relationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.38,0:18:25.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn,\Nhave you gone insane?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.41,0:18:27.36,Default,,0,0,0,,My God\Npeople can see you!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.41,0:18:29.48,Default,,0,0,0,,What if I had been\Nthe paperboy?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.55,0:18:31.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Get in there!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.38,0:18:34.19,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you\Nthinking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.99,0:18:38.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.39,0:18:40.70,Default,,0,0,0,,- Evelyn!\N- Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.76,0:18:44.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, what we really need\Ninstead of this baloney...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.80,0:18:48.87,Default,,0,0,0,,is an assertiveness\Ntraining class for\NSouthern women.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.93,0:18:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's a contradiction\Nin terms, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.57,0:18:55.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Especially you, sweetheart.\NYou're livin' in the Dark Ages.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.06,0:19:21.67,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hi, honey.\NI need one of those.\N- Hi!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.73,0:19:24.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Mmm, you smell good too.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.57,0:19:26.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I need one of these.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.67,0:19:29.62,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh, this looks good!\N- Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.68,0:19:31.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, indeedy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.79,0:19:43.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.46,0:19:47.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you come in?\Nand sit down at the table...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.69,0:19:51.64,Default,,0,0,0,,- and have dinner with me?\N- I'm sorry.\NThe game's almost over.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.70,0:19:54.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I just want to see\Na little bit of it.\NWhy you so dressed up?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.60,0:19:57.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Honey, don't get in the way.\NScoot over a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.24,0:20:02.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.88,0:20:05.88,Default,,0,0,0,,If I'd answered the door\Nwearing only cellophane,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.95,0:20:09.26,Default,,0,0,0,,would you still be\Nwatching the baseball game?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.32,0:20:13.06,Default,,0,0,0,,No, honey. I'd probably\Nbe checking you into\Na looney bin.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.37,0:20:39.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, sugar.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.68,0:20:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,- How's my dumplin'?\N- Trick or treat!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.68,0:20:43.63,Default,,0,0,0,,You 're not gonna throw\Nthem hissy-fits, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.68,0:20:46.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Happy Halloween!\NOh, no. No, no, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.99,0:20:49.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You 're meaner\Nthan a damn snake.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.15,0:20:51.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad\Nyou're feeling better.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.22,0:20:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,- Get back in bed\N- Good thing\Nyour eyesight's failing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.10,0:21:07.24,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey!\N- Mmm. Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.31,0:21:10.72,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey.\N- I was hopin'\Nyou'd be here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.78,0:21:14.85,Default,,0,0,0,,My roommate, Mrs. Otis,\Nsaid I could visit her family,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.91,0:21:16.86,Default,,0,0,0,,but I said,\N"Thank you kindly,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.92,0:21:19.56,Default,,0,0,0,,but I think I might have\Nmy own visitor."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.62,0:21:21.62,Default,,0,0,0,,And here you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.69,0:21:23.97,Default,,0,0,0,,- Well, sit down.\N- Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.02,0:21:27.56,Default,,0,0,0,,And doughnuts to boot!\NYou can't beat that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.63,0:21:30.47,Default,,0,0,0,,- Well, help yourself,\NMrs. Threadgoode.\N- Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.20,0:21:32.24,Default,,0,0,0,,How's your friend?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.30,0:21:34.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- Mrs. Otis?\N- Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.37,0:21:37.32,Default,,0,0,0,,- Well, not so good.\N- Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.37,0:21:40.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like I won't be\Ngettin' home for quite a while,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.17,0:21:43.62,Default,,0,0,0,,and I sure miss it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.68,0:21:46.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Funny what you miss\Nwhen you're away from home.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.01,0:21:49.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I miss\Nthe smell of coffee...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.48,0:21:52.29,Default,,0,0,0,,and bacon fryin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.35,0:21:56.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, what I wouldn't give for a\Nplate of fried green tomatoes...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.92,0:21:59.63,Default,,0,0,0,,like we used to have\Nat the cafe.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.69,0:22:02.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Ooh!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.63,0:22:08.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I never told you\Nabout the cafe,\Ndid I?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.77,0:22:10.72,Default,,0,0,0,,No, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.77,0:22:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, well...\Nnow let me back up a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.44,0:22:20.69,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, Idgie never\Nquite got over losing Buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.02,0:22:26.09,Default,,0,0,0,,She hardly\Never come home.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.15,0:22:29.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Only Big George\Nknew how to find her.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.09,0:22:33.84,Default,,0,0,0,,She just didn't seem to care\Nabout anythin' anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.89,0:22:35.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, one summer day
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.74,0:22:42.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on in, honey.\NShe's right down here.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.61,0:22:46.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- Here? Okay.\N- Uh-huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.12,0:22:48.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll see you,\NGrady Kilgore,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.82,0:22:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'll\Nraise you twenty.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.95,0:22:53.52,Default,,0,0,0,,You ain't got nothin'!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.59,0:22:56.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe I do and\Nmaybe I don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.96,0:23:01.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Put your money where\Nyour mouth is, Mr. Sheriff.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.24,0:23:07.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, look what\Nthe cat drug in!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.94,0:23:11.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I came to talk to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.88,0:23:14.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna have to wait.\NI'm busy.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.31,0:23:16.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Grady, this\Nis your big chance.\NYou in or out?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.98,0:23:19.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll make you\Na rich man.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.48,0:23:22.48,Default,,0,0,0,,You just bluffin' again\Nas usual
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.55,0:23:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid you're gonna\Nhave to excuse Idgie.\NShe's goin' home for dinner.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.62,0:23:27.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- Say good-bye, Idgie.\N- Where you goin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.86,0:23:32.24,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where the hell you goin'\Nwith my money?\N- We're goin' home!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.30,0:23:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,- Who are you to boss me around?\N- The one holdin' your money!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.30,0:23:38.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Give it back.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.30,0:23:40.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, get in the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.31,0:23:45.55,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.\NI'll get in the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.61,0:23:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You win!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.18,0:23:51.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.21,0:23:52.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Sucker!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.85,0:23:54.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll leave when I want!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.95,0:23:58.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know how you can break\Nyour mother's heart like you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.82,0:24:00.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not doin' anything\Nto my mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.06,0:24:03.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no? Why do you think\NI'm here for the summer?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.69,0:24:07.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Your mother was so worried,\Nshe thought I might be able\Nto talk some sense into you.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.13,0:24:09.47,Default,,0,0,0,,But you're too busy\Nbeing selfish!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.53,0:24:12.51,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you\Ntalkin' about?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.57,0:24:16.28,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not the only one\Nwho lost Buddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.34,0:24:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,We all miss him...
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.51,0:24:21.39,Default,,0,0,0,,but turning your back on\Nyour family is not gonna help.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.75,0:24:25.82,Default,,0,0,0,,What's he got to do\Nwith anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.88,0:24:30.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I oaks like you 're\Nthe one with the problem\Nforgetting my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.39,0:24:36.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Why just ten miles a way ..
Dialogue: 0,0:24:36.96,0:24:38.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Down by the river,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.93,0:24:41.17,Default,,0,0,0,,there lurks\Na den of the devil...
Dialogue: 0,0:24:48.45,0:24:51.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's turn to page 53\Nin our hymnal.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.83,0:25:00.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoo-hoo!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:00.90,0:25:05.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Big George thought\NI might find you here.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.57,0:25:13.42,Default,,0,0,0,,If you give me a chance,\Na chance to get to know you,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.48,0:25:17.22,Default,,0,0,0,,maybe it'll be fun!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:17.28,0:25:20.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Fun?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:20.75,0:25:24.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie,just spend\Nsome time with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.09,0:25:26.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Please?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:26.09,0:25:28.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Suit yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.73,0:25:31.40,Default,,0,0,0,,You sure you don't\Nwanna back out?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.46,0:25:34.67,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's not too late.\N- I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.73,0:25:37.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, hold this.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.07,0:25:41.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me now,\Nyou like trains?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.84,0:25:45.65,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes.\N- Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.71,0:25:49.62,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll get along\Njust fine!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.12,0:25:54.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, did we\Nluck out tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.49,0:25:59.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Hop in.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.79,0:26:02.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Hop?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:02.39,0:26:05.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh. Give me\Nyour hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.50,0:26:07.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Put your foot\Nup there.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.28,0:26:19.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold that.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.31,0:26:23.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Ooo-ooo!\NLook at all this!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:27.72,0:26:31.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you think we should\Nget off the train?\NIt's startin' to move.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.36,0:26:35.17,Default,,0,0,0,,No. The fun\Njust started!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:38.50,0:26:40.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.97,0:26:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, sometimes I get\Na little dizzy lookin' down.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.27,0:26:47.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't look down.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.85,0:27:04.63,Default,,0,0,0,,- What are you doin'?\N- Come on. Look.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.69,0:27:07.60,Default,,0,0,0,,They're throwin'\Naway food!
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.43,0:27:14.07,Default,,0,0,0,,You talk about\N"give unto others."
Dialogue: 0,0:27:26.42,0:27:28.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- More!\N- Give me some.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:53.38,0:27:56.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, time to get off.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:57.39,0:27:59.37,Default,,0,0,0,,We gotta jump.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.42,0:28:02.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Lump?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:02.09,0:28:05.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah jump. The next stop's\Nfive miles down the tracks.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:05.23,0:28:07.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't wanna walk\Nthat far back.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.30,0:28:10.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you crazy?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:10.23,0:28:12.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not kiddin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:12.67,0:28:16.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:28:16.41,0:28:18.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I give up. Jump.-
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.94,0:28:22.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll tell Mama I'm not\Na good influence on you-
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.28,0:28:24.56,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll never jump,\Nwill you?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.58,0:28:29.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't say "never"\Nto me.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.77,0:28:44.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.41,0:29:00.02,Default,,0,0,0,,- You all right?\N- I'm fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:00.08,0:29:03.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.72,0:29:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.92,0:29:08.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Does this hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:08.33,0:29:11.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.16,0:29:13.47,Default,,0,0,0,,- We better get you\Nto a doc-doctor.\N- Shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.53,0:29:15.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Which way is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:15.70,0:29:19.31,Default,,0,0,0,,About two miles\Ndown the tracks.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:19.37,0:29:21.61,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.\Nlet's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.41,0:29:26.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll never be able\Nto carry me that far.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.98,0:29:29.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.\NNever say never.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:29.75,0:29:33.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not carryin' you.\NYou're walkin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.82,0:29:44.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Julian.\NI owe you one.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:56.47,0:29:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh. Ow.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.48,0:30:02.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Aren't you ready yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:02.11,0:30:04.22,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.28,0:30:09.35,Default,,0,0,0,,This doesn't have anything\Nto do with trains, does it?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.25,0:30:12.49,Default,,0,0,0,,You like honey?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.56,0:30:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, I like honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:14.59,0:30:16.59,Default,,0,0,0,,- Fresh honey?\N- Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:16.66,0:30:20.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Me too.\NThere it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:20.26,0:30:24.47,Default,,0,0,0,,There what... is?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.53,0:30:28.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll see soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.38,0:30:34.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Now... stay here.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.68,0:30:37.63,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter what happens,\Ndon't move.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:37.68,0:30:40.96,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you\Ngonna do?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.95,0:31:18.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:52.66,0:31:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Here you are, madam.\NThis is for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.33,0:32:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did you do that?\NYou could have been killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:00.76,0:32:04.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.33,0:32:07.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you want\Nthe honey?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:07.10,0:32:10.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I got it\Njust for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:10.51,0:32:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right.\NI do it all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.04,0:32:16.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I never get stung,\Nhonest.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.88,0:32:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't be\Nmad at me, Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.95,0:32:22.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie.\NI'm not mad at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:22.92,0:32:25.49,Default,,0,0,0,,No foolin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.30,0:32:35.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it bad,\Nwhat I did?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:35.06,0:32:37.40,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:37.47,0:32:39.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought I might\Nbe crazy or somethin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:39.70,0:32:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.57,0:32:46.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I've heard there were people\Nwho could charm bees.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.31,0:32:49.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I've just never\Nseen it done...\Nbefore today.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:51.85,0:32:56.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You're just a bee charmer,\NIdgie Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:56.29,0:33:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what you are,\Na bee charmer.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.82,0:33:03.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, you want\Nto taste it?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:09.70,0:33:12.44,Default,,0,0,0,,"Satan started to laugh\Nat job's devotion.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:12.50,0:33:17.75,Default,,0,0,0,,"He bet God that job would\Nnever have so much faith...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:17.81,0:33:19.92,Default,,0,0,0,,"if he didn't have\Nso many blessings.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:19.98,0:33:23.86,Default,,0,0,0,,"He went on and on\Nso long and so much\Nthat God finally agreed...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.91,0:33:26.62,Default,,0,0,0,,"to let Satan\Nput Job to a test.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.68,0:33:29.82,Default,,0,0,0,,"Suddenly from bein'\Non top of the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:29.89,0:33:33.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Job was plunged down\Ninto the deepest pits\Nof misery."
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.56,0:33:38.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Surprise!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:40.56,0:33:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie Threadgoode!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.57,0:33:44.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Tonight we're gonna have\Na real party.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:44.57,0:33:46.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Drink this... and then,\Nwe're gonna play some poker.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:46.87,0:33:50.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know\Nhow to play poker\Nand I never drink...
Dialogue: 0,0:33:50.81,0:33:52.81,Default,,0,0,0,,but thank you anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:57.95,0:34:00.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Here comes the windup.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:00.52,0:34:02.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Burn that ball in here.\NBurn 'em in here!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:02.92,0:34:07.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- Right in the pocket.\N- I don't know how\Nto bat.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:07.36,0:34:10.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And you don't drink,\Neither.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:10.23,0:34:13.34,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's gonna be a spitter.\N- Hold the bat and swing
Dialogue: 0,0:34:13.40,0:34:15.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Spitter?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:15.20,0:34:18.41,Default,,0,0,0,,- She gonna spit at me?\N- She's gonna spit on the ball
Dialogue: 0,0:34:18.47,0:34:21.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Swing that bat!\NTake another crack at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:21.74,0:34:23.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna take\Nanother crack at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.97,0:34:27.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Get 'em in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:34.68,0:34:37.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Now run, Ruth.\NRun!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:37.55,0:34:39.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on\Naround the bases!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:39.62,0:34:41.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't kiss everybody.\NRun!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.69,0:34:44.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I have never had\Nso much fun...
Dialogue: 0,0:34:44.79,0:34:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,in my whole life.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:47.20,0:34:50.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I even got a home run.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.57,0:34:53.55,Default,,0,0,0,,A clean one\Nat that!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.60,0:34:56.81,Default,,0,0,0,,A straight beats\Nthree of a kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:01.91,0:35:06.15,Default,,0,0,0,,You know,\Npoker isn't half bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:06.22,0:35:08.39,Default,,0,0,0,,What's your mother\Ngonna say...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:08.45,0:35:11.83,Default,,0,0,0,,when she sees us both...\Ndrunk?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:11.89,0:35:15.80,Default,,0,0,0,,- You gotta stop worrying\Nabout what people think.\N- I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:15.86,0:35:17.86,Default,,0,0,0,,You've always done\Nthe right thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:17.93,0:35:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You took care of your daddy,\Nthe preacher, when he took sick.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:21.43,0:35:25.31,Default,,0,0,0,,You take care of all the kids\Nover at the church school.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:25.37,0:35:28.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna\Ntake care of your mama.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:28.17,0:35:31.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm gonna marry\Nthe man I'm supposed to.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:31.77,0:35:34.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You gettin' married?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:34.11,0:35:38.39,Default,,0,0,0,,As soon as\Nthe summer's over.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.92,0:35:45.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, am I\Ngonna miss you.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.69,0:35:48.83,Default,,0,0,0,,This is\Nthe best birthday...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:48.89,0:35:51.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I ever had.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.42,0:36:06.66,Default,,0,0,0,,No sir!\NWhew!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:06.72,0:36:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Mama Jamison,\Nyou put that down.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:11.06,0:36:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, my Lord!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:20.17,0:36:22.31,Default,,0,0,0,,During these next few weeks,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:22.37,0:36:26.72,Default,,0,0,0,,we will be learning to reclaim\Nour own power as women!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:26.77,0:36:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Hallelujah!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:28.94,0:36:33.72,Default,,0,0,0,,And tonight, we're gonna\Nbegin to explore...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:33.78,0:36:35.99,Default,,0,0,0,,our own femaleness...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.05,0:36:40.62,Default,,0,0,0,,by examining the source\Nof our strength...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.69,0:36:43.07,Default,,0,0,0,,and our separateness.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:43.12,0:36:45.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Our vaginas.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:47.06,0:36:49.87,Default,,0,0,0,,So if ya'll will just\Nslip off your panties...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:49.93,0:36:53.47,Default,,0,0,0,,and straddle your mirrors.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:53.53,0:36:56.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Ms. Couch!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:56.27,0:36:59.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Ms. Couch!
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.77,0:37:04.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, I need to be excused\Nfor a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:04.21,0:37:08.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Um, Missy, could you come\Nwith me to the ladies' room?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:08.35,0:37:12.09,Default,,0,0,0,,- Do you find this threatening?\N- Uh, well, um-
Dialogue: 0,0:37:12.15,0:37:16.29,Default,,0,0,0,,- do you have a problem\Nwith your sexuality?\N- No, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:16.36,0:37:19.40,Default,,0,0,0,,But I do have a problem\Nwith my girdle.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:44.15,0:37:47.72,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, fried chicken!\NMy favorite.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:53.59,0:37:55.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:55.80,0:37:58.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.93,0:38:03.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Those classes I've been taking\Naren't helpin' us one bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:03.50,0:38:06.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go to Florida...
Dialogue: 0,0:38:06.24,0:38:08.58,Default,,0,0,0,,like when\Nwe got married.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:08.64,0:38:11.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Kyle's gone,\Nbusy with his own life.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.05,0:38:14.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It'd be\Njust the two of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:14.11,0:38:17.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, honey, it's just\Nthe two of us here now.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:17.12,0:38:19.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, you got a good scald\Non that chicken!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:19.89,0:38:22.89,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'm tellin' you,\Nthat's really good.\N- Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:22.96,0:38:24.91,Default,,0,0,0,,We could rent a boat...
Dialogue: 0,0:38:24.96,0:38:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,and drift around\Nin the hot sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:28.70,0:38:30.81,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you\Nthink about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.86,0:38:33.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just gettin' used to it\Nbeing quiet around here.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:33.93,0:38:37.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Honey, if those classes\Naren't doin' you any good,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:37.77,0:38:40.75,Default,,0,0,0,,then don't go to 'em.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:40.81,0:38:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone needs a miracle\Nin their life.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:43.48,0:38:47.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn, game's\Nblacked out!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:55.52,0:38:58.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Yoo-hoo,\NMrs. Threadgoode?
Dialogue: 0,0:38:58.19,0:39:01.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey. Evelyn!
Dialogue: 0,0:39:01.66,0:39:03.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you like it?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:03.93,0:39:07.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Oooh! Well,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:07.37,0:39:10.32,Default,,0,0,0,,- who did it for ya,\Ndarlin'?\N- Believe it or not,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:10.37,0:39:12.32,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a student,\Na little bitty thing,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:12.37,0:39:15.98,Default,,0,0,0,,no bigger than a midget\Nfrom the beauty college.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:16.04,0:39:19.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Sometimes they come out here\Nand do our hair for free...
Dialogue: 0,0:39:19.45,0:39:22.26,Default,,0,0,0,,just for the practice,\Nyou know.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:22.32,0:39:26.86,Default,,0,0,0,,- Is Ed with ya?\N- No, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:26.92,0:39:30.66,Default,,0,0,0,,His aunt said she didn't\Nwant visitors anymore,\Nespecially us.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:30.72,0:39:34.96,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a shame.\NI know he feels bad,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:35.03,0:39:38.03,Default,,0,0,0,,but Lord if he'll\Ntalk to me about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:42.97,0:39:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:45.27,0:39:48.25,Default,,0,0,0,,- Merry Christmas.\N- Merry Christmas.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:49.71,0:39:52.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Threadgoode-
Dialogue: 0,0:39:54.49,0:39:57.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you go stirrin' up\Nno trouble for Miss Ruth now.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:57.99,0:40:00.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes, ma'am.\N- Don't "yes, ma'am" me.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:00.36,0:40:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,You can stay in my house\Nas long as you want,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:02.40,0:40:05.11,Default,,0,0,0,,but don't treat me\Nlike you treat your mama.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:05.16,0:40:07.57,Default,,0,0,0,,- Grandma!\N- Yes, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:34.76,0:40:36.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi there.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:36.76,0:40:40.67,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yes?\N- Uh, is Ruth at home?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:40.73,0:40:42.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Who's callin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:42.94,0:40:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You just tell her\Nit's the bee charmer\Nfrom Alabama.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:47.31,0:40:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth,
Dialogue: 0,0:40:50.34,0:40:54.15,Default,,0,0,0,,there's some bee person\Nhere to see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:07.09,0:41:10.73,Default,,0,0,0,,- Idgie.\N- Hi.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:10.80,0:41:14.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You got a real nice home,\Nreal nice things and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:14.47,0:41:16.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm,\Nthank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:16.54,0:41:21.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama said to give you\Nthis pie.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.07,0:41:23.85,Default,,0,0,0,,So-
Dialogue: 0,0:41:25.91,0:41:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie Threadgoode,\Nhow are ya?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:30.98,0:41:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You look so...\Nso grown up.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:35.66,0:41:40.23,Default,,0,0,0,,All the guys\Nmust be wild about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:40.29,0:41:44.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me,\Ndo you have a fella yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:44.13,0:41:48.58,Default,,0,0,0,,A... couple.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:48.63,0:41:51.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't decided\Non any.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:51.07,0:41:53.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Grady's the most\Npersistent, but-
Dialogue: 0,0:41:53.07,0:41:55.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- Grady Kilgore?\N- Don't say it\Nso loud.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:56.04,0:41:58.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth, honey\Nwho's down there?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:59.85,0:42:01.83,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey-\N- Well-
Dialogue: 0,0:42:01.88,0:42:04.36,Default,,0,0,0,,- What happened to you?\N- Nothin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:04.42,0:42:06.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothin'!\NWhere'd you get the shiner?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:06.62,0:42:08.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I-\NWho's down there?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:08.62,0:42:11.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- You'd better leave now.\N- Did he hit you?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:11.86,0:42:15.57,Default,,0,0,0,,- Did he beat you?\NSomebody's got to talk to him.\N- Idgie.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:15.63,0:42:17.77,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're not\Ngonna do anything.\N- I'm gonna kill him.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:17.83,0:42:19.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna have\Na conversation\Nwith him about...
Dialogue: 0,0:42:19.97,0:42:22.75,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're not gonna\Ndo anything.\N- ...pickin' on\Nsomebody his own size.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:22.80,0:42:25.28,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not gonna do\Nanything, understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:25.34,0:42:27.55,Default,,0,0,0,,If you care about me,\Nif you really do,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:27.61,0:42:31.52,Default,,0,0,0,,you'll turn around\Nand leave this minute.\NYou understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:44.52,0:42:48.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, what'd\Nshe want?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:50.30,0:42:53.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:03.38,0:43:07.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth's a grown woman,\Nand she knows what's\Nbest for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:08.01,0:43:11.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Mmm, I'm not so sure\Nabout that.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:12.02,0:43:14.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:14.12,0:43:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Grady.\NHi.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:16.49,0:43:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,- Idgie,will you dance\Nwith me?\N- No.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:20.19,0:43:22.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.\NIt's only a dance.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:26.67,0:43:29.74,Default,,0,0,0,,- Miss Idgie Threadgoode...\N- Get your butt\Noff the ﬂoor.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:29.80,0:43:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you dance\Nwith me?
Dialogue: 0,0:43:35.27,0:43:40.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I will not dance with you,\Nand I will not marry you.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:40.08,0:43:43.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Go marry Gladys Moats.\NShe just adores you.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:43.32,0:43:47.29,Default,,0,0,0,,But she did fall on her\Nhead when she was a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:48.49,0:43:51.80,Default,,0,0,0,,You're just a goofy girl,\NIdgie, a goofy girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:51.86,0:43:53.86,Default,,0,0,0,,- Who're you callin'\Na goof?\N- Ow-ow-ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:43:53.93,0:43:57.10,Default,,0,0,0,,- Who you callin' a goof?\N- Stop that before I get mad\Nand hurt ya.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:57.16,0:43:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah.\NYou try it.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:59.40,0:44:02.94,Default,,0,0,0,,- Grady!\N- There now,\Nyou give up?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:03.00,0:44:04.98,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I'll never\Ngive up!
Dialogue: 0,0:44:05.04,0:44:09.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Grady finally got dizzy\Nand give up.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:09.64,0:44:14.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Try as they might, none of them\Nfellas could tame Idgie.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:14.98,0:44:17.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Now,\Na little while later,
Dialogue: 0,0:44:17.25,0:44:21.03,Default,,0,0,0,,a letter\Ncome from Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:25.59,0:44:28.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.\NIt's an obituary.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:28.36,0:44:31.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no, honey,\NRuth's mother died.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:31.86,0:44:33.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:33.87,0:44:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,And this\Nis from the Bible.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:36.04,0:44:38.61,Default,,0,0,0,,It's from\Nthe book of Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:38.67,0:44:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,"And Ruth said,\Nwhither thou goest, I will go;
Dialogue: 0,0:44:43.98,0:44:46.32,Default,,0,0,0,,"where thou lodgest,\NI will lodge;
Dialogue: 0,0:44:46.38,0:44:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,thy people\Nshall be my people."
Dialogue: 0,0:45:07.93,0:45:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,All right Julian,\Nyou and Big George wait here.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:23.58,0:45:27.26,Default,,0,0,0,,- Mama died.\N- I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:29.86,0:45:33.77,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm pregnant.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:51.08,0:45:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Julian, I got another box here\Nwhen you're done!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:05.42,0:46:07.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I never seen anybody\Nwith so many hats.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:07.53,0:46:09.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't we put\Nthree in one box?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:09.76,0:46:12.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think we can fit\Nall these in the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:12.77,0:46:15.88,Default,,0,0,0,,We're gonna need a separate\Ntruck for all your stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:15.94,0:46:17.89,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell\Nis going on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:17.94,0:46:19.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like your wife's\Nleavin' you, mister.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:19.94,0:46:24.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- Sure she is.\NDon't you touch her!\NLet go.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:24.84,0:46:28.45,Default,,0,0,0,,You bastard!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:28.51,0:46:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Put her down!
Dialogue: 0,0:46:32.72,0:46:36.53,Default,,0,0,0,,See, the thing is,\Nyou might upset Big George.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:36.59,0:46:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,And he's crazy
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.06,0:46:43.17,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no tellin'\Nwhat he might do.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:03.95,0:47:07.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on,\Nget outta here.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:17.43,0:47:20.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:20.13,0:47:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on! Hey hey!\NCome on now!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:23.50,0:47:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go. Come on.\NYou okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:26.57,0:47:29.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's get Miss Ruth\Nand get outta here.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:29.24,0:47:32.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Miss Ruth.\NCome on.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:34.48,0:47:38.45,Default,,0,0,0,,If you ever touch her again,\NI'll kill you.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:44.12,0:47:47.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I sure as hell\Nscared him, didn't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:47.43,0:47:50.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah you sure scared him.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:50.13,0:47:53.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda,\Nthe amazing Amazon woman!
Dialogue: 0,0:47:53.16,0:47:55.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:55.23,0:47:58.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda! Towanda!
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.94,0:48:03.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn?\NEvelyn!
Dialogue: 0,0:48:03.94,0:48:06.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!\NI'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:06.18,0:48:08.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I was just lookin'\Nat the pictures, Missy.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:08.31,0:48:11.66,Default,,0,0,0,,They have the greatest\Nstories in that magazine,\Ndon't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:11.72,0:48:14.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Will I see you\Nin group tonight?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:14.15,0:48:16.69,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll be talking about\Nmasturbation.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:16.75,0:48:20.86,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I don't think so.\NI think I've had enough\Nlearnin' for the time bein'.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:20.93,0:48:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\NThank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:24.76,0:48:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!\NExcuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:27.57,0:48:30.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Screw you!
Dialogue: 0,0:48:37.31,0:48:39.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me,\Nyoung man.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:39.41,0:48:43.22,Default,,0,0,0,,There was no reason for you\Nto be so rude to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:43.28,0:48:45.85,Default,,0,0,0,,- Get away from me,\Nyou fat cow.\N- What did you call me?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:45.92,0:48:48.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Beat it,\Nyou old bitch.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:48.49,0:48:51.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you being\Nso mean to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:51.52,0:48:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,What did I ever\Ndo to you-
Dialogue: 0,0:48:54.76,0:48:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't understand!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:06.57,0:49:09.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at my Stove Top!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:16.11,0:49:18.95,Default,,0,0,0,,BOO!
Dialogue: 0,0:49:19.02,0:49:23.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, honey, what in the world\Nis the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:23.69,0:49:26.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:28.19,0:49:31.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:31.63,0:49:34.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.\NI need some exercise.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:42.67,0:49:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, you tell me what's\Nbotherin' you, sugar.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:48.61,0:49:53.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I just-\NI just feel so useless.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:53.25,0:49:57.10,Default,,0,0,0,,So-\NSo powerless.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:57.16,0:50:02.11,Default,,0,0,0,,- Everybody goes\Nthrough that.\N- But I can't stop eatin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:02.16,0:50:07.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Every day I try and try\Nand every day I go off.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:10.13,0:50:13.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I hide candy bars\Nall over the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:13.24,0:50:16.22,Default,,0,0,0,,A candy bar ain't\Ngonna hurt ya none.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:16.27,0:50:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,One, no.\NBut 10 or 11?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:22.01,0:50:25.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't even look\Nat my own vagina.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:25.45,0:50:28.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't help ya\Non that one.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:28.99,0:50:33.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I wish I had the courage\Nto get it over with and\Nget really fat.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:37.33,0:50:41.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Mrs. Threadgoode,\NI just-
Dialogue: 0,0:50:41.83,0:50:46.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm too young to be old\Nand I'm too old to be young.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.24,0:50:51.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe I'm just\Ngoin' crazy.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:52.68,0:50:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You get hot ﬂashes?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:55.95,0:50:57.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Sometimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:57.95,0:51:01.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You get the sweats\Nand your hearts\Nstarts a-poundin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:02.05,0:51:04.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- How did you know?\N- Simple, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:04.46,0:51:08.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're going through\Nthe change.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:08.23,0:51:12.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I used to burst into tears\Nfor no reason at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:14.40,0:51:16.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You need\Nsome hormones.\NHmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:51:16.77,0:51:20.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe some\NStresstabs number 4\Nfor good measure.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:20.44,0:51:23.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- Really? Is that all?\N- Sure, honey.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:23.98,0:51:26.32,Default,,0,0,0,,You get yourself\Nsome hormones.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:26.38,0:51:29.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Then you get outta\Nthe house and get a job.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:31.25,0:51:33.70,Default,,0,0,0,,With your\Npretty complexion...
Dialogue: 0,0:51:33.75,0:51:37.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll bet you'll be\Ngreat with cosmetics.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:38.92,0:51:42.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I know how\Nyou feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:42.56,0:51:46.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I was about your age\Nwhen I had my child.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:46.06,0:51:48.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I went through\Nthe change of life.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.63,0:51:53.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- I didn't know\Nyou had a child.\N- Yes, I did.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:53.34,0:51:56.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Albert.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:56.37,0:52:00.98,Default,,0,0,0,,When he was born,\Nthe doctor said it would\Nbe best if I didn't see him.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:01.05,0:52:05.16,Default,,0,0,0,,He said his mind\Nwould never develop\Npast the age of five,
Dialogue: 0,0:52:05.22,0:52:08.20,Default,,0,0,0,,and I should just put him\Nin an institution...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:08.25,0:52:12.93,Default,,0,0,0,,because the burden\Nof raisin' a child like that\Nwould be too great.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:14.13,0:52:18.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I thought\Nabout Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:20.53,0:52:22.87,Default,,0,0,0,,She always said...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:22.93,0:52:26.38,Default,,0,0,0,,there was a separate\NGod for children.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:26.44,0:52:31.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Sol smiled at him and\NI asked for the baby.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:31.41,0:52:36.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, how could anybody think\Nthat sweet, precious baby...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:36.18,0:52:38.42,Default,,0,0,0,,could ever\Nbe a burden?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:38.48,0:52:42.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, from the minute\Nhe was born, Albert\Nwas the joy of my life,
Dialogue: 0,0:52:42.85,0:52:45.89,Default,,0,0,0,,the Lord's\Ngreatest gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:45.96,0:52:50.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't believe\Nthere was a purer soul\Never lived on this earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:50.60,0:52:53.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I had him with me\Ntill he was 30.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:53.63,0:52:57.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Then he went to sleep\Nand didn't wake up.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:59.30,0:53:02.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Sometimes I can't wait to get\Nto heaven to see him again.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:05.68,0:53:07.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:07.68,0:53:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit!\NIt's a boy!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:13.15,0:53:16.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I think a prayer\Nof thanksgivin'\Nwould be in order.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:16.92,0:53:20.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Goddamn it to hell,\Nson-of-a-bitch, she did it!\NHere's to Ruth!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:20.99,0:53:25.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie always did have a way\Nwith words around the reverend.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.96,0:53:29.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, Ruth had a baby
Dialogue: 0,0:53:29.53,0:53:32.27,Default,,0,0,0,,She named him Buddy-\NBuddy junior.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:32.34,0:53:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Papa went out and borrowed\Nmoney so Ruth and Idgie\Ncould start a cafe,
Dialogue: 0,0:53:37.54,0:53:39.78,Default,,0,0,0,,the Whistle Stop 6.22%.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:16.01,0:54:18.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Miss Idgie\Ncan you get the door?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:18.35,0:54:21.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.\NBig George.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:22.02,0:54:25.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Miss Ruth, me and the missus\Nwant to thank you...
Dialogue: 0,0:54:25.39,0:54:27.56,Default,,0,0,0,,for sendin' that soup\Nover last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:27.63,0:54:31.87,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'll pay you\Nwhen I get ahead.\N- You don't owe me, Ocie.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:31.93,0:54:34.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- Thank you.\N- I'm just glad\Nthey're better.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:34.67,0:54:38.35,Default,,0,0,0,,- How is this,\Nby the way?\N- It's good, very good.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:38.40,0:54:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not happy\Ntill I see clean plates.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:44.54,0:54:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't go on,\NIdgie.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:47.14,0:54:49.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm talking to you\Nas a friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:49.51,0:54:53.98,Default,,0,0,0,,- There's people in this town,\Npaying customers too-\N- There you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:54.05,0:54:57.69,Default,,0,0,0,,But some people\Ndon't like you...
Dialogue: 0,0:54:57.76,0:54:59.93,Default,,0,0,0,,sellin' to coloreds.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:59.99,0:55:01.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Here you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:02.03,0:55:05.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell you what.\NNext time those\N"some people" come here,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:06.00,0:55:08.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna ask if they\Ndon't want anybody to know...
Dialogue: 0,0:55:08.50,0:55:10.67,Default,,0,0,0,,who they are\Nunder those sheets...
Dialogue: 0,0:55:10.74,0:55:14.85,Default,,0,0,0,,when they go marchin'\Nin those stupid parades,
Dialogue: 0,0:55:14.91,0:55:17.75,Default,,0,0,0,,how come they\Ndon't have sense\Nto change their shoes?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:17.84,0:55:21.19,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hold on there.\N- Y'all ain't foolin' anybody.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:21.24,0:55:25.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd recognize those size 14\Nclodhoppers you got anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:25.52,0:55:28.66,Default,,0,0,0,,- Just a minute, Idgie.\N- More pie, Grady?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:28.72,0:55:31.22,Default,,0,0,0,,No, thank you, Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:31.29,0:55:34.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie, I'll talk\Nto the boys.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:34.92,0:55:37.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You just keep them\Non out back there, ya hear?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:37.16,0:55:41.94,Default,,0,0,0,,- Bye, Ruth.\N- Bye, Grady.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.63,0:55:44.08,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna\Nget yourself in\Na heap of trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:44.13,0:55:48.14,Default,,0,0,0,,What, Grady?\NHe's harmless.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:48.20,0:55:52.24,Default,,0,0,0,,You shoulda seen that\Nbig ox down by the river.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:52.31,0:55:56.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Three solid days,\Ndrunk as a dog,\Ncryin' like a baby...
Dialogue: 0,0:55:56.41,0:55:59.19,Default,,0,0,0,,'cause Joe,\Nthat ol' colored man\Nthat raised him, died.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:59.25,0:56:01.20,Default,,0,0,0,,- Remember that, Sipsey?\N- Yes'm.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:01.25,0:56:03.96,Default,,0,0,0,,- He sure ain't' jokin'\Nnow, is he, son?\N- No, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:04.02,0:56:06.40,Default,,0,0,0,,He won't even sit\Nin the same room\Nand have a meal today.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:06.46,0:56:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't make no sense.\NBig ox like Grady won't sit\Nnext to a colored child,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:11.46,0:56:14.91,Default,,0,0,0,,but he eats eggs-\NShoot right out\Nof a chicken's ass.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:39.82,0:56:42.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Smokey,\Nlet's go for a walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:51.47,0:56:54.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry about\Nspillin' my food, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:54.30,0:56:57.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll just\Nhead on.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:06.68,0:57:09.72,Default,,0,0,0,,See that piece\Nof land over there?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:09.79,0:57:12.60,Default,,0,0,0,,See it?\NThat used to be a lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:12.66,0:57:14.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:14.72,0:57:16.67,Default,,0,0,0,,This one November,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:16.73,0:57:18.68,Default,,0,0,0,,all these ducks\Ncome by...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:18.73,0:57:22.01,Default,,0,0,0,,and they landed\Non that lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:22.06,0:57:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Then the temperature\Ndropped so fast, the\Nwhole lake just froze.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:26.24,0:57:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Then the ducks\Ntook off and took\Nthe lake with 'em.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:29.34,0:57:32.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that lake's somewhere\Nin Georgia, the way I hear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:32.21,0:57:34.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on now.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:48.49,0:57:50.97,Default,,0,0,0,,God bless you,\Nma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:19.96,0:58:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, try this.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:26.00,0:58:30.04,Default,,0,0,0,,- So what do you think?\N- They're okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:30.10,0:58:33.81,Default,,0,0,0,,- The truth.\N- Well-
Dialogue: 0,0:58:36.41,0:58:39.19,Default,,0,0,0,,They're terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:39.24,0:58:44.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, well, don't be shy.\NTell me how you feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:44.25,0:58:46.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:59.46,0:59:01.63,Default,,0,0,0,,What'd you go\Nand do that for?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:04.43,0:59:07.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I just thought you needed\Na little coolin' off.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:07.77,0:59:11.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:25.22,0:59:28.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Try these.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:32.46,0:59:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I think we need\Nto make a little paste.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:54.22,0:59:56.96,Default,,0,0,0,,What in the name\Nof Christmas are\Nyou two doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:57.02,0:59:58.97,Default,,0,0,0,,She's tryin'\Nto teach me\Nhow to cook.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:59.02,1:00:01.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at those\Nfried green tomatoes.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:06.00,1:00:10.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You better stop this.\NI'm gonna have to arrest you\Nfor disorderly conduct.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:10.40,1:00:12.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Arrest us then.\NLet me handle this.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:12.94,1:00:15.22,Default,,0,0,0,,- All right.\N- Grady.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:17.01,1:00:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha-ha-ha!
Dialogue: 0,1:00:19.58,1:00:23.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Arrest us.\NGo ahead, arrest us.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:23.81,1:00:28.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth, I have to say it.\NI believe Idgie's been\Na bad influence on ya.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:28.25,1:00:31.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I agree.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:10.39,1:01:13.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be back in a minute.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:13.56,1:01:15.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Y'all keep the show\Ngoing till then.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:15.70,1:01:17.74,Default,,0,0,0,,We ain't goin'\Nnowhere.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:27.28,1:01:31.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I ain't scared\Nof you! No, sir!
Dialogue: 0,1:01:31.39,1:01:34.80,Default,,0,0,0,,You should be.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:44.54,1:01:46.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Mind your manners, boy!
Dialogue: 0,1:01:55.81,1:01:58.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Grady,
Dialogue: 0,1:01:58.25,1:02:01.49,Default,,0,0,0,,what does Gladys think\Nof you stayin' out late...
Dialogue: 0,1:02:01.55,1:02:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,and losin' your money to me\Nin poker night after night?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:06.69,1:02:09.53,Default,,0,0,0,,She likes it\Njust fine.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:14.10,1:02:16.74,Default,,0,0,0,,- They got Big George.\N- Idgie!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:16.80,1:02:19.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- Let go of him!\N- Let me handle this!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:19.37,1:02:23.25,Default,,0,0,0,,We seen how you treat\Nyour niggers around here\Nand we don't like it.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:23.31,1:02:27.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm the law in these parts.\NI don't care what you\Nlike or don't like.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:27.64,1:02:29.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Turn him loose.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:29.68,1:02:32.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't get riled up,\Nnigger lover.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:32.95,1:02:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You deaf or somethin'?\NI said, let him go!
Dialogue: 0,1:02:37.49,1:02:40.47,Default,,0,0,0,,- Before you get yourselves\Nin a whole lot of trouble!\N- Calm down.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:40.52,1:02:43.30,Default,,0,0,0,,We wanted to have\Na little get-together...
Dialogue: 0,1:02:43.36,1:02:46.34,Default,,0,0,0,,and make sure we see\Neye to eye on some things.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:46.40,1:02:49.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You hear me now?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:49.90,1:02:51.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's let him go, boys.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:52.00,1:02:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,We've had enough fun\Nfor one night.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:53.77,1:02:55.72,Default,,0,0,0,,- Turn him loose.\N- Come on.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:55.77,1:02:57.75,Default,,0,0,0,,No, you're gonna\Nget in trouble.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:00.31,1:03:02.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, now,\Nthat's more like it.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:02.91,1:03:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Seems I don't recognize\Nany of you boys.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:05.92,1:03:08.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Y'all ain't from Whistle Stop,\Nare you?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:11.19,1:03:13.26,Default,,0,0,0,,This ought to do it.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:13.32,1:03:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to thank you,\NMiss Idgie.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:16.39,1:03:21.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Forget it.\NYou'd have done\Nthe same for me.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:21.63,1:03:25.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Try to get some sleep.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:30.24,1:03:33.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Who the hell\Nwere those assholes?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:33.41,1:03:38.69,Default,,0,0,0,,They's just some old boys\Nfrom Georgia come over here\Nto put a scare in you.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:38.75,1:03:41.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, it worked.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:41.25,1:03:43.96,Default,,0,0,0,,One of 'em was here\Nthe other day for something,
Dialogue: 0,1:03:44.02,1:03:46.56,Default,,0,0,0,,seen you sellin' food\Nto coloreds.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:46.62,1:03:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,They decided to come back,\Nshake you up a bit.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:50.76,1:03:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I told 'em we don't need\Nanybody from Georgia\Ncomin' over here...
Dialogue: 0,1:03:54.26,1:03:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,tellin' us what\Nwe can or cannot do.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:56.87,1:04:02.05,Default,,0,0,0,,They won't be back.\NI guaran-gol-damn-tee\Nyou that.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:02.11,1:04:05.18,Default,,0,0,0,,One other thing,\Nlittle Miss Smarty-pants,
Dialogue: 0,1:04:05.24,1:04:09.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not wear a size 14 shoe...
Dialogue: 0,1:04:09.58,1:04:13.15,Default,,0,0,0,,and I don't\Nmuch care for parades,
Dialogue: 0,1:04:13.22,1:04:16.83,Default,,0,0,0,,bedsheets or otherwise.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:00.88,1:05:04.23,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey there!\N- You got to come quick.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:04.28,1:05:07.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, the show\Nhas hardly begun.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:07.52,1:05:10.26,Default,,0,0,0,,You got to come quick now.\NYou hear me?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:12.99,1:05:15.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- Run, get help!\NRun, quick!\N- Where's the baby?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:15.36,1:05:17.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:36.81,1:05:42.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, sir.\NI don't believe you\Nshould be goin' anywhere...
Dialogue: 0,1:05:42.42,1:05:44.99,Default,,0,0,0,,with Ruth's baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:28.67,1:06:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That's my husband,\Nbut I haven't seen\Nhim in months.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:33.51,1:06:36.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I heard he got run over\Nby a Brinks armored truck.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:36.81,1:06:38.85,Default,,0,0,0,,What's he done?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:38.91,1:06:42.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothin' that we know of.\NWe're tryin' to find out\Nwhat's been did to him.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:42.98,1:06:46.48,Default,,0,0,0,,He told his hired man he was\Ncomin' to see his wife and baby,
Dialogue: 0,1:06:46.56,1:06:50.57,Default,,0,0,0,,but he ain't never\Nshowed up back home.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:50.63,1:06:53.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Hell, I told him\Nif he showed up in this town,
Dialogue: 0,1:06:53.40,1:06:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,we'd all have known.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:55.60,1:06:58.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks a little sissified\Nto me.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:58.10,1:07:02.11,Default,,0,0,0,,From what I hear,\Nmost you boys in Georgia...
Dialogue: 0,1:07:02.17,1:07:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,are a little light\Non your feet
Dialogue: 0,1:07:03.67,1:07:06.84,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the way\NI heard it.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:06.91,1:07:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Could I interest you\Nin some pie?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:09.11,1:07:13.02,Default,,0,0,0,,No, ma'am, but that\Nbarbecue sure smells good.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:13.08,1:07:16.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Best damn barbecue\Nin the state of Alabama.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:45.75,1:07:48.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Here you go.\NThat's your 4th one today.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:48.45,1:07:51.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I swear you're about\Nto eat up all my barbecue.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:51.35,1:07:54.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Sit down.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:05.34,1:08:08.01,Default,,0,0,0,,You sure you ain't\Nnever seen this man, boy?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:08.08,1:08:11.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir, and I already told ya,\NI ain't never seen him.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:11.78,1:08:14.28,Default,,0,0,0,,You'd do anything for\NMiss Idgie, wouldn't ya, boy?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:16.19,1:08:18.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:21.36,1:08:24.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Would ya kill for her?\NDid ya kill for her?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:32.34,1:08:34.48,Default,,0,0,0,,No, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:34.54,1:08:39.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, now, maybe\None of these days\Nyou'll tell the truth.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:41.41,1:08:44.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Just remember, we hang\Nlyin' niggers in Georgia...
Dialogue: 0,1:08:44.18,1:08:47.16,Default,,0,0,0,,just as fast as\Nthey do in Alabama.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:47.22,1:08:51.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir, I remember.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:28.56,1:09:33.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:33.06,1:09:38.01,Default,,0,0,0,,- What are ya\Ndoin' in here?\N- No milk in the house.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:38.07,1:09:40.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Where were you?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:43.82,1:09:46.10,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,1:09:52.99,1:09:54.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't believe me.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:54.99,1:09:59.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Right now, I don't know\Nwhat to believe.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:02.03,1:10:05.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Believe me when I tell ya\NI don't want ya to move out.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:30.93,1:10:34.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:34.33,1:10:38.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks, I've been\Nout here all day.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:05.23,1:11:07.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me.\NI was waiting for that space.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:07.70,1:11:12.65,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah? Tough!\N- Face it, lady,\Nwe're younger and faster.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:33.19,1:11:36.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:39.60,1:11:42.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha-ha-ha-ha!
Dialogue: 0,1:11:42.70,1:11:47.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah!\NWhooo!
Dialogue: 0,1:11:51.98,1:11:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda!
Dialogue: 0,1:11:59.32,1:12:02.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:02.19,1:12:04.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoooo!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:07.89,1:12:11.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- Help, someone!\N- What are you doing?\NAre you crazy?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:11.46,1:12:16.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Face it, girls.\NI'm older, and I\Nhave more insurance.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:25.01,1:12:28.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I never get mad,\NMrs. Threadgoode.\NNever!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:28.71,1:12:31.28,Default,,0,0,0,,The way I was raised\Nit was bad manners.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:31.35,1:12:34.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I got mad\Nand it felt terrific.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:34.59,1:12:37.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I felt like I could beat\Nthe shit outta all those punks!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:40.96,1:12:43.17,Default,,0,0,0,,so they'll explode\Nwhen you open 'em.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:43.23,1:12:47.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll ban all fashion models\Nwho weigh less than 130 pounds.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:49.51,1:12:53.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll give half the military\Nbudget to people over 65...
Dialogue: 0,1:12:53.14,1:12:55.88,Default,,0,0,0,,and declare wrinkles\Nsexually desirable.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:55.95,1:13:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Towanda, righter of wrongs,\Nqueen beyond compare!
Dialogue: 0,1:13:00.65,1:13:03.96,Default,,0,0,0,,How many of them\Nhormones you takin', honey?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:19.44,1:13:21.94,Default,,0,0,0,,what I can't\Nunderstand is...
Dialogue: 0,1:13:22.01,1:13:25.62,Default,,0,0,0,,how in the hell\Nyou can hit someone...
Dialogue: 0,1:13:25.68,1:13:27.92,Default,,0,0,0,,six times\Nby accident.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:27.98,1:13:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Ed, don't make\Nsuch a big deal about it.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:37.42,1:13:41.96,Default,,0,0,0,,- What the hell is this?\N- A low cholesterol meal.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:42.03,1:13:43.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Happy Valentine's.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:47.23,1:13:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,My God!\NAre you tryin' to kill me?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:50.23,1:13:53.51,Default,,0,0,0,,If I was gonna kill ya,\NI'd use my hands.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:10.42,1:14:13.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm worried about\Nmy little friend Evelyn.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:13.09,1:14:15.66,Default,,0,0,0,,She said her husband...
Dialogue: 0,1:14:15.73,1:14:18.04,Default,,0,0,0,,will just be watching\Nhis sports on TV...
Dialogue: 0,1:14:18.09,1:14:21.26,Default,,0,0,0,,and she has an urge to hit him\Nin the head with a baseball bat.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:21.33,1:14:24.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Hell, that\Nseems normal to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:24.27,1:14:26.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hi Janeen.\N- Mm-hmm
Dialogue: 0,1:14:26.34,1:14:28.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Threadgoode, would\Nyou like some crudites?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:29.82,1:14:31.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Mommy! Mommy!
Dialogue: 0,1:14:39.33,1:14:41.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Buddy.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:41.33,1:14:43.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Everybody\Noutta the way.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:43.34,1:14:47.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Give him here.\NLet him go. I've got him.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:49.08,1:14:51.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on. You're\Ngonna be all right.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:51.34,1:14:53.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Open the door!
Dialogue: 0,1:14:53.75,1:14:57.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Put him in the car.\NIt's all right, honey
Dialogue: 0,1:15:19.04,1:15:20.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I can understand...
Dialogue: 0,1:15:21.01,1:15:23.55,Default,,0,0,0,,having a funeral\Nfor an arm.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:23.61,1:15:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I just don't know why\Nshe insists on callin'\Nhim "Stump."?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:27.21,1:15:30.21,Default,,0,0,0,,She say everybody else gonna\Nbe callin' him that...
Dialogue: 0,1:15:30.28,1:15:34.39,Default,,0,0,0,,so we might just as well\Nbe the first.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:34.45,1:15:38.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, ice cream\Nand cake for everybody.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:38.69,1:15:40.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:44.77,1:15:48.78,Default,,0,0,0,,My daddy always used to say\Nthere was a separate God\Nfor children.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:52.64,1:15:56.18,Default,,0,0,0,,The good Lord was watchin'\Nover stump that day.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:57.64,1:16:02.95,Default,,0,0,0,,this poor, weak woman\Nwith promises of\Nliquor and money,
Dialogue: 0,1:16:03.02,1:16:06.76,Default,,0,0,0,,and she lost control\Nof her senses momentarily.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:06.82,1:16:09.82,Default,,0,0,0,,When her husband came back\Nto get her and take her home,
Dialogue: 0,1:16:09.89,1:16:14.53,Default,,0,0,0,,you and your colored man\Nmurdered him in cold blood.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:15.73,1:16:17.33,Default,,0,0,0,,No, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:17.40,1:16:22.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, where were you on the\Nnight of September 30, 1933?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:22.74,1:16:25.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I was at the town hall\Ndoing a show.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:25.11,1:16:28.22,Default,,0,0,0,,- And after that?\N- I was at\Nmy mother's house.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:28.28,1:16:30.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah?\NWho was with you?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:30.88,1:16:35.23,Default,,0,0,0,,- Just Big George and myself\N- What about your mother?\NCan she confirm that?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:35.28,1:16:37.56,Default,,0,0,0,,No, sir.\NShe died a year ago.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:37.62,1:16:40.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to hear that.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:40.19,1:16:43.90,Default,,0,0,0,,But do you expect 12 intelligent\Nmen to believe you,
Dialogue: 0,1:16:43.96,1:16:46.60,Default,,0,0,0,,although one witness is dead and\Nthe other is a colored man,
Dialogue: 0,1:16:46.66,1:16:50.07,Default,,0,0,0,,known to be a worthless,\Nno-good, lying nigger?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:50.13,1:16:52.41,Default,,0,0,0,,You expect these men\Nto take your word for it...
Dialogue: 0,1:16:52.47,1:16:55.14,Default,,0,0,0,,just because\Nyou say so?
Dialogue: 0,1:16:55.20,1:16:59.74,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right,\Nyou gump-faced, blown-up,\Nbaboon-assed bastard!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:59.81,1:17:03.28,Default,,0,0,0,,One more outburst\Nlike that...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:03.34,1:17:06.84,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'll hold you\Nin contempt of court.\NYou understand?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:06.91,1:17:09.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:14.90,1:17:16.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I do.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:18.93,1:17:23.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You have information\Nabout the whereabouts...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:23.24,1:17:26.85,Default,,0,0,0,,of Idgie Threadgoode\Nand her colored man,\Nknown as Big George,
Dialogue: 0,1:17:26.91,1:17:30.69,Default,,0,0,0,,on the night\Nof September 30, 1933?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:30.75,1:17:32.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir,\NI do.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:32.78,1:17:35.23,Default,,0,0,0,,It has been\Nsuggested here...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:35.28,1:17:38.75,Default,,0,0,0,,that she and her colored man\Nwere at her mother's house.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:38.82,1:17:43.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- Can you confirm that?\N- No, sir.\NThat is a lie.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:43.13,1:17:45.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, shit.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:45.93,1:17:49.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It has been my habit\Nto write all the dates...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:49.23,1:17:52.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Of the activities of\Nthe church in my Bible.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:52.23,1:17:56.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I show that the night\Nof September 30, 1933...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:56.97,1:18:00.01,Default,,0,0,0,,was the start of our\Nannual revival...
Dialogue: 0,1:18:00.08,1:18:02.86,Default,,0,0,0,,down at the\NBaptist campground.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:02.91,1:18:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Sister Threadgoode\Nwas there...
Dialogue: 0,1:18:05.08,1:18:09.12,Default,,0,0,0,,along with her hired man,\NGeorge Pullman,
Dialogue: 0,1:18:09.19,1:18:13.33,Default,,0,0,0,,who was in charge of the\Nbarbecue as he has been...
Dialogue: 0,1:18:13.39,1:18:16.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- for the last ten years.\N- Objection.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:16.13,1:18:20.67,Default,,0,0,0,,That doesn't mean anything.\NMurder could've taken place any\Ntime the next couple of clays.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:20.73,1:18:25.77,Default,,0,0,0,,- Have you ever been to one\Nof our revivals, sir?\N- Well, no.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:25.84,1:18:27.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you attend church\Nregularly, sir?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:27.97,1:18:30.18,Default,,0,0,0,,'Course I do.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:30.24,1:18:34.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. Well, maybe if you\Nattended one of our revivals,
Dialogue: 0,1:18:34.84,1:18:37.22,Default,,0,0,0,,you'd know\Nthey last three days...
Dialogue: 0,1:18:37.28,1:18:39.62,Default,,0,0,0,,and three nights,\NYour Honor.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:41.88,1:18:44.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Approach the bench.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:44.92,1:18:49.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Percy, it don't look like\Nyou got a case at all.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:52.46,1:18:54.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoo!
Dialogue: 0,1:19:01.84,1:19:04.75,Default,,0,0,0,,See you in church,\NSister?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:05.64,1:19:07.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Reverend.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:07.94,1:19:12.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe he\Nactually swore on a Bible.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:12.31,1:19:14.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, not really.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:14.32,1:19:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,If that judge\Nhad looked closer,
Dialogue: 0,1:19:16.39,1:19:19.46,Default,,0,0,0,,he'd have seen it was really\Na copy of Moby Dick.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:21.49,1:19:25.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- But why did he do it?\N- For the sheer joy of\Nseeing you in church again...
Dialogue: 0,1:19:25.96,1:19:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,which I suggested to him\Nmight be your penance.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:28.86,1:19:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,- You didn't promise him,\Ndid you?\N- Yes, ma'am, I did.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:31.57,1:19:33.52,Default,,0,0,0,,And I never\Nbreak my word.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:33.57,1:19:37.95,Default,,0,0,0,,If I live 1,000 years,\NI will never forgive you.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:38.01,1:19:42.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know what's worse,\Nchurch or jail.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:53.16,1:19:56.30,Default,,0,0,0,,There now.\NDon't you look pretty?
Dialogue: 0,1:19:56.36,1:19:58.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes, honey.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:58.56,1:20:03.24,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll have me\Nlookin' like Ginger Rogers\Nbefore you're done.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:03.30,1:20:07.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't let Mr. Dunaway see me.\NHe's liable to go wild.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:35.64,1:20:38.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn, what in the hell\Nare you doing?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:38.74,1:20:41.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I need some light\Nand air.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:41.71,1:20:44.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Why don't you take\None of your walks\Nor your jog...
Dialogue: 0,1:20:44.98,1:20:48.52,Default,,0,0,0,,or whatever it is\Nyou do?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:48.59,1:20:51.50,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no dinner\Neither!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:51.55,1:20:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed, you have any idea\Nwhy I've been goin'\Nto all these classes?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:56.06,1:20:59.60,Default,,0,0,0,,- No.\N- I've been trying to save\Nour marriage.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:59.66,1:21:01.70,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the point\Nof my tryin'...
Dialogue: 0,1:21:01.77,1:21:06.45,Default,,0,0,0,,if you're gonna sit on\Nyour butt drinking beer...
Dialogue: 0,1:21:06.50,1:21:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,and watching baseball,\Nbasketball, football...
Dialogue: 0,1:21:09.41,1:21:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,bowling and hockey\Nand golf...
Dialogue: 0,1:21:12.61,1:21:16.49,Default,,0,0,0,,and Challenge\Nof the Gladiators?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:22.19,1:21:26.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Couch, I'm Sue,\NMrs. Otis' daughter-in-law.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:26.79,1:21:30.24,Default,,0,0,0,,How are you?\NI've heard about you\Nfrom Mrs. Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:30.29,1:21:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,She is so sweet. She's been\Nlookin' after my mother-in-law.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:34.06,1:21:36.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, how is\NMrs. Otis doin',\Nby the way?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:36.90,1:21:41.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Much better, thank you.\NIt takes time getting used\Nto a strange place.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:41.44,1:21:45.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad to hear it.\NMrs. Threadgoode's\Nbeen anxious to get home.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:45.54,1:21:49.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Couch, Mrs. Threadgoode\Ndoesn't have a house anymore.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:49.81,1:21:53.28,Default,,0,0,0,,- They tore\Nthat down.\N- What?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:53.35,1:21:57.59,Default,,0,0,0,,They had to.\NIt was falling apart,\Nand it was condemned.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:57.65,1:22:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:00.66,1:22:04.87,Default,,0,0,0,,- Does she know that?\N- No, well, we didn't see\Nany point in telling her.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:04.93,1:22:07.43,Default,,0,0,0,,It would just break her heart,\Npoor old thing
Dialogue: 0,1:22:07.50,1:22:11.45,Default,,0,0,0,,But I am so glad\NI got a chance to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:11.50,1:22:14.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You take care of yourself now.\NBye-bye.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:24.67,1:23:26.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Evelyn. hey!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:27.04,1:23:29.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey-
Dialogue: 0,1:23:29.58,1:23:31.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you like\Nmy roses?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:32.02,1:23:35.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Since I can't get home\Nto look at my own roses...
Dialogue: 0,1:23:35.42,1:23:37.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I made myself\Na paper garden.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:37.85,1:23:41.35,Default,,0,0,0,,- Got everything\Nbut the bugs.\N- They're lovely.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:41.42,1:23:44.70,Default,,0,0,0,,- You been here long?\N- Happy birthday!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:44.76,1:23:47.26,Default,,0,0,0,,- Oh!\N- I shouldn't\Nhave woken you up.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:47.33,1:23:51.61,Default,,0,0,0,,'Course you should've.\NDon't you never let me sleep\Nthrough a visitor's day, honey.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:51.67,1:23:56.42,Default,,0,0,0,,- I look forward to them all week.\N- So do I, Mrs. Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:56.47,1:23:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh! I can't believe\Nyou remembered.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:59.88,1:24:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You made me\Nfried green tomatoes!
Dialogue: 0,1:24:06.52,1:24:08.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Mmm!\NThey're delicious.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:08.62,1:24:11.97,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's your recipe.\NAre they cold?\N- No.\NThey're just the way...
Dialogue: 0,1:24:12.02,1:24:16.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- we used to have 'em\Nat the Whistle Stop Cafe.\N- Mmm!
Dialogue: 0,1:24:16.36,1:24:20.31,Default,,0,0,0,,You couldn't be sweeter to me\Nif you was my own daughter.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:20.36,1:24:22.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's your napkin.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:22.60,1:24:24.64,Default,,0,0,0,,And wait-wait-wait.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:24.70,1:24:27.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Queen, queen.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:30.44,1:24:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You know,\NI don't feel 83.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:34.64,1:24:38.78,Default,,0,0,0,,It sorta slipped up on me.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:40.88,1:24:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I never expected\Nto live this long.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:44.39,1:24:50.00,Default,,0,0,0,,'Course, the Lord takes us home\Nwhen he wants us.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:59.00,1:25:02.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:02.71,1:25:05.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I was thinking\Nabout Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:05.11,1:25:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,After the trial\Nwas over,
Dialogue: 0,1:25:07.98,1:25:10.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything went back\Nto normal...
Dialogue: 0,1:25:10.25,1:25:14.03,Default,,0,0,0,,till that fall\Nwhen Ruth lost her appetite.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:14.08,1:25:16.65,Default,,0,0,0,,By the time Doc Hadley\Nlooked at her,
Dialogue: 0,1:25:16.72,1:25:20.93,Default,,0,0,0,,he said the cancer was so bad\Nshe only had a couple of weeks.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:20.99,1:25:23.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, we moved her\Nto the Threadgoode house...
Dialogue: 0,1:25:23.79,1:25:28.64,Default,,0,0,0,,and put her downstairs\Nso she'd be more comfortable.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:28.70,1:25:33.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Sipsey moved in with her\Nand never left her side.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:33.27,1:25:35.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on, baby\NI'm right here.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:35.47,1:25:40.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie just prayed\Nfor a miracle.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:59.43,1:26:02.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, listen to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:02.97,1:26:05.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Make sure he graduates.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:05.57,1:26:09.78,Default,,0,0,0,,And don't... let him\Ncome to the funeral.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:09.84,1:26:12.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't want him going\Nthrough that mess.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:12.58,1:26:15.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you quit talkin'\Nlike that?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:15.95,1:26:18.45,Default,,0,0,0,,What funeral?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:18.51,1:26:20.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You're gonna be back on\Nyour feet feelin' just fine...
Dialogue: 0,1:26:20.95,1:26:23.62,Default,,0,0,0,,in just a few days.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:23.69,1:26:26.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Just you wait.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:26.66,1:26:29.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, what's the matter,\Nson?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:35.63,1:26:39.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,\Nlet's go for a walk.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:40.00,1:26:41.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you get\Ninto a fight?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:41.67,1:26:44.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I got punched\Nin the nose.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:44.44,1:26:47.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't play\Nlike everyone else.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:48.01,1:26:51.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I ever tell you the\Nstory about... the oysters?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:51.61,1:26:54.09,Default,,0,0,0,,All the millions of 'em\Njust lying around-
Dialogue: 0,1:26:54.15,1:26:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,- And God put sand in one of 'em,\Nand it makes a pearl.\N- Oh.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:00.76,1:27:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I ever tell you about\NEva's three-legged dog?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:03.49,1:27:05.60,Default,,0,0,0,,How it never felt sorry\Nfor itself...
Dialogue: 0,1:27:05.66,1:27:09.30,Default,,0,0,0,,and howl ought to be\Nsmarter than a dumb dog\Nand not feel sorry for myself.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:11.10,1:27:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,You listen to everything\NI say, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:14.50,1:27:17.48,Default,,0,0,0,,You get real mad at me\Nwhen I don't.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:17.54,1:27:19.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,
Dialogue: 0,1:27:21.71,1:27:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,you know about\Nyour mama.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:24.78,1:27:27.28,Default,,0,0,0,,She's sick.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:27.35,1:27:29.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:30.92,1:27:34.37,Default,,0,0,0,,See, now is the time\Nfor courage.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:34.42,1:27:38.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess you already know\Nthat there are...
Dialogue: 0,1:27:38.19,1:27:41.19,Default,,0,0,0,,angels masqueradin' as people\Nwalkin' around this planet,
Dialogue: 0,1:27:41.26,1:27:44.43,Default,,0,0,0,,and your mom's\Nthe bravest one of those.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:48.70,1:27:50.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Come here.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:58.51,1:28:00.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama, I can hit!\NYou should see me.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:00.98,1:28:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie, she hit me in\Nthe back with a curveball.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:03.85,1:28:06.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't duck,\Nand I hardly cried.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:06.09,1:28:09.56,Default,,0,0,0,,She hit you?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:09.63,1:28:13.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, she did that\Nto me once too,
Dialogue: 0,1:28:13.70,1:28:16.48,Default,,0,0,0,,but I think\NI did cry.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:18.37,1:28:22.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama, I'm sorry\Nif you're sad.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:22.41,1:28:24.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,
Dialogue: 0,1:28:24.77,1:28:27.88,Default,,0,0,0,,give me a big kiss then,\Nand I'll never be sad again.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:35.42,1:28:38.33,Default,,0,0,0,,And you best not be sad\Nneither.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:38.39,1:28:41.63,Default,,0,0,0,,You understand?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:41.69,1:28:43.64,Default,,0,0,0,,You promise?
Dialogue: 0,1:28:43.69,1:28:45.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Promise.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:45.80,1:28:49.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Attaboy.\NYou go and wash up.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:13.56,1:29:15.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Sweet baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:19.56,1:29:22.84,Default,,0,0,0,,You two\Nbe alone now.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:23.53,1:29:27.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, girl.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:29.71,1:29:31.78,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:33.71,1:29:36.78,Default,,0,0,0,,That's nice.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:37.78,1:29:41.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you do one thing\Nfor me?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:41.55,1:29:45.16,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah, anything.\N- Be good to yourself.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:45.22,1:29:48.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Even...
Dialogue: 0,1:29:48.22,1:29:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,settle down if\Nyou can find someone...
Dialogue: 0,1:29:50.83,1:29:53.57,Default,,0,0,0,,who can beat you\Nin poker.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:01.27,1:30:06.24,Default,,0,0,0,,There's so many things\NI want to say to you.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:06.31,1:30:08.85,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:09.68,1:30:12.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I love your stories.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:12.42,1:30:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me a story,\NIdgie.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:18.22,1:30:22.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:22.12,1:30:25.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on,\Nyou old' bee charmer.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:25.29,1:30:28.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me\Na good tall tale.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:30.37,1:30:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me the one\Nabout the lake.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:35.37,1:30:40.01,Default,,0,0,0,,- What lake?\N- The one...\Nthat used to be here.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:42.14,1:30:44.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:46.15,1:30:49.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that was\Njust a lie.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:49.79,1:30:52.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I know that, fool.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:52.62,1:30:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me anyway.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:54.76,1:30:58.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me the story.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:59.73,1:31:03.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,1:31:05.20,1:31:07.68,Default,,0,0,0,,one time...
Dialogue: 0,1:31:07.74,1:31:10.55,Default,,0,0,0,,there was this lake.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:14.98,1:31:19.36,Default,,0,0,0,,And, uh, it was\Nright outside of town.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:19.42,1:31:24.87,Default,,0,0,0,,We used to go\Nfishin' and swimmin'\Nand canoein' in it.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:24.92,1:31:28.16,Default,,0,0,0,,And see,\None November...
Dialogue: 0,1:31:28.22,1:31:30.53,Default,,0,0,0,,this big ﬂock\Nof ducks...
Dialogue: 0,1:31:30.59,1:31:35.63,Default,,0,0,0,,came in and landed\Non that lake and, uh,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:35.70,1:31:40.55,Default,,0,0,0,,and then the temperature\Ndropped so fast that the\Nlake just froze right there.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:40.60,1:31:42.88,Default,,0,0,0,,And the, uh,
Dialogue: 0,1:31:42.94,1:31:46.72,Default,,0,0,0,,the ducks, they...
Dialogue: 0,1:31:46.78,1:31:50.96,Default,,0,0,0,,ﬂew off, you see,\Nand took that lake with 'em.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:51.01,1:31:54.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And, uh.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:54.32,1:31:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Now they say that lake is\Nsomewhere over in Georgia.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:59.39,1:32:02.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you imagine?
Dialogue: 0,1:33:00.15,1:33:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right,\Nhoney.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:03.49,1:33:06.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Let her go.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:06.09,1:33:09.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Let her go.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:09.53,1:33:13.77,Default,,0,0,0,,You know,\NMiss Ruth was a lady.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:13.83,1:33:17.11,Default,,0,0,0,,And a lady\Nalways knows...
Dialogue: 0,1:33:17.17,1:33:20.17,Default,,0,0,0,,when to leave.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:25.67,1:33:29.78,Default,,0,0,0,,When I think on our\Ndeparted sister, Ruth Jamison,
Dialogue: 0,1:33:29.85,1:33:32.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm reminded of our\NLord's Sermon on the Mount...
Dialogue: 0,1:33:33.02,1:33:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,and how his teachings-
Dialogue: 0,1:33:35.55,1:33:40.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It's funny how strong\NRuth affected everyone.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:40.06,1:33:43.47,Default,,0,0,0,,even Smokey Lonesome.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:43.53,1:33:46.20,Default,,0,0,0,,When he died\Na few years back...
Dialogue: 0,1:33:46.26,1:33:48.97,Default,,0,0,0,,he had one possession\Non him,
Dialogue: 0,1:33:49.03,1:33:51.64,Default,,0,0,0,,A picture of Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:53.00,1:33:57.11,Default,,0,0,0,,He was in love with her\Nfrom the first time he saw her.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:57.17,1:34:00.05,Default,,0,0,0,,We all were.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:06.02,1:34:08.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I shouldn't\Na-told you this.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:10.42,1:34:14.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate death.\NIt scares me so.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:14.46,1:34:17.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Death is nothin'\Nto be afraid of!
Dialogue: 0,1:34:17.06,1:34:20.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at me. I'm at\Nthe jumpin'-off place,
Dialogue: 0,1:34:20.20,1:34:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,and I ain't afraid\None bit.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:23.50,1:34:27.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Ninny,\Nyou're so brave.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:28.77,1:34:32.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Ruth and Idgie were brave,\Nnot me.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:32.78,1:34:36.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be afraid\Nof death if I was you.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:36.21,1:34:41.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd be more afraid of driving\Nin rush-hour traffic.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:36.37,1:36:39.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, honey.\NLook what I got you.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:39.44,1:36:41.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah...
Dialogue: 0,1:36:41.54,1:36:45.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed, how sweet!
Dialogue: 0,1:36:45.07,1:36:47.52,Default,,0,0,0,,- Lilies!\NMy favorite.\N- Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:47.58,1:36:50.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I know.\NSometimes I even amaze myself.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:50.78,1:36:54.89,Default,,0,0,0,,- What's the occasion?\N- Oh, honey,\NI just...
Dialogue: 0,1:36:54.95,1:36:57.93,Default,,0,0,0,,feel sorry about\Nthe past few months.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:57.99,1:37:02.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know what\Nyou're really up to and\Nwhat's going on with you,
Dialogue: 0,1:37:02.06,1:37:06.48,Default,,0,0,0,,but I guess I could've been\Nmore helpful with your job\Nand everything, you know.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:07.70,1:37:09.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, why are you...
Dialogue: 0,1:37:09.63,1:37:12.61,Default,,0,0,0,,puttin' up this wall\Nwhere you just tore one down?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:12.67,1:37:15.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...\NI changed my mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:15.87,1:37:18.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't mean to seem\Ndense or anything,
Dialogue: 0,1:37:18.71,1:37:22.95,Default,,0,0,0,,- but what's changed?\N- The air and the light.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:25.31,1:37:27.92,Default,,0,0,0,,- Ed-\N- Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:27.98,1:37:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,You remember how\Nyou used to tell me...
Dialogue: 0,1:37:30.52,1:37:33.26,Default,,0,0,0,,you always wanted\Ntwo women in your house?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:33.32,1:37:35.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:35.69,1:37:37.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:37.43,1:37:39.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,1:37:39.53,1:37:42.48,Default,,0,0,0,,what if I was\Nthe younger of the two?
Dialogue: 0,1:37:42.53,1:37:46.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't believe\NI get your drift.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:46.14,1:37:50.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I want something\Nmore than I've ever\Nwanted anything before.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:50.74,1:37:53.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to bring\NMrs. Threadgoode...
Dialogue: 0,1:37:53.58,1:37:55.79,Default,,0,0,0,,to our home.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:55.84,1:37:58.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I want her\Nto live here with us.
Dialogue: 0,1:37:58.55,1:38:01.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to give her the love\Nshe's given me.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:01.12,1:38:05.30,Default,,0,0,0,,You're kiddin' me, aren't you?\NI'm absolutely serious.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:05.35,1:38:10.20,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why I'm puttin' the\Nwall to Kyle's room back up.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:10.26,1:38:13.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, honey, this isn't\Nsomething you're just go and do.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:13.40,1:38:16.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean,\Nshe's an old woman.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:16.13,1:38:19.37,Default,,0,0,0,,What if she got sick?\NWho's gonna take care of her?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:19.44,1:38:21.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I will!
Dialogue: 0,1:38:21.20,1:38:23.20,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't leave her\Nin that place.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:23.27,1:38:27.18,Default,,0,0,0,,She's not a stray cat.\NHell, she isn't even family.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:27.24,1:38:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,- She's family to me.\N- Now, Evelyn.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:31.15,1:38:34.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:34.28,1:38:36.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Honey?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:36.22,1:38:38.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, look...
Dialogue: 0,1:38:38.29,1:38:42.53,Default,,0,0,0,,have you mentioned this\Nharebrained idea to her?
Dialogue: 0,1:38:42.59,1:38:45.66,Default,,0,0,0,,- Not yet.\N- Well, good!
Dialogue: 0,1:38:45.73,1:38:48.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Then we'll just pretend\Nit never happened.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:48.26,1:38:51.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm making my own money.\NI'll pay for everything.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:51.37,1:38:54.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You don't have to do\Na thing.
Dialogue: 0,1:38:55.00,1:38:57.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Evelyn...
Dialogue: 0,1:38:57.57,1:39:00.05,Default,,0,0,0,,it's never\Ngonna happen.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:00.11,1:39:02.78,Default,,0,0,0,,So just forget\Nabout it.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:04.38,1:39:07.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you ever\Nsay "never" to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:16.09,1:39:18.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone helped put a mirror\Nup in front of my face,
Dialogue: 0,1:39:18.96,1:39:21.57,Default,,0,0,0,,and I didn't like\Nwhat I saw one bit.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:21.63,1:39:25.48,Default,,0,0,0,,You know what I did?\NI changed.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:25.53,1:39:29.44,Default,,0,0,0,,And that someone...\Nwas Mrs. Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:29.51,1:39:34.02,Default,,0,0,0,,She needs my love\Nand care, and I'm\Ngonna give it to her.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:35.78,1:39:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,If you'll excuse me,\NI have to go to the gym.
Dialogue: 0,1:39:44.35,1:39:47.39,Default,,0,0,0,,And if you won't listen\Nto reason...
Dialogue: 0,1:39:47.46,1:39:51.10,Default,,0,0,0,,there's always Towanda.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:05.87,1:40:08.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Nin-
Dialogue: 0,1:40:11.51,1:40:14.55,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:14.62,1:40:17.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Those are her things,\NMrs. Threadgoode's things!
Dialogue: 0,1:40:17.42,1:40:20.53,Default,,0,0,0,,- What are you doing in here?\NWhere's Mrs. Threadgoode?\N- Who?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:20.59,1:40:23.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Threadgoode!\NThe woman who lives here.\NAre you deaf?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:23.49,1:40:26.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, miss.\NAll they told me...
Dialogue: 0,1:40:26.46,1:40:30.67,Default,,0,0,0,,was that the woman who lived\Nin here died this morning.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:32.53,1:40:34.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh. my God!
Dialogue: 0,1:40:34.74,1:40:39.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Wha- What\Nare you sayin'?
Dialogue: 0,1:40:39.14,1:40:41.31,Default,,0,0,0,,She died early\Nthis morning.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:41.38,1:40:45.73,Default,,0,0,0,,They were shorthanded\Nso they asked me to take\Nall this stuff down.
Dialogue: 0,1:40:45.78,1:40:48.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That? all I know.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:07.67,1:41:09.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop that!
Dialogue: 0,1:41:09.67,1:41:12.05,Default,,0,0,0,,What is the matter\Nwith you people?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:12.11,1:41:15.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't you wait a goddamn day,\Nfor Chrissake?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:15.11,1:41:18.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you have no respect?\NThese are her things!
Dialogue: 0,1:41:18.18,1:41:22.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, but they told me\Nto get this room ready\Nfor another patient.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:22.42,1:41:25.63,Default,,0,0,0,,She may be just\Nanother patient to you,
Dialogue: 0,1:41:25.69,1:41:29.80,Default,,0,0,0,,- but she was my friend,\Nand I loved her.\N- I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:29.86,1:41:31.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm just\Nfollowing orders.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:31.86,1:41:34.81,Default,,0,0,0,,- What is going on?\N- Why didn't\Nyou call me?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:34.86,1:41:38.21,Default,,0,0,0,,- You could've called me before\Nyou sent that idiot-\N- I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:38.27,1:41:40.94,Default,,0,0,0,,It never occurred to me\Nthat you would take it\Nthis hard.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:41.00,1:41:44.64,Default,,0,0,0,,- I didn't even get\Nto tell her good-bye.\N- Oh, I know.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:44.71,1:41:48.68,Default,,0,0,0,,These things are difficult,\Nbut she died peacefully\Nin her sleep.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:48.74,1:41:52.02,Default,,0,0,0,,To tell you the truth,\NI thought you'd be happy\Nfor Mrs. Threadgoode.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:52.08,1:41:55.12,Default,,0,0,0,,- Happy?\N- Why, yes!\NThis is what she wanted.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:55.18,1:41:57.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What?\NTo be dead?
Dialogue: 0,1:41:57.19,1:41:59.73,Default,,0,0,0,,No, to go home.\NYou just missed her.
Dialogue: 0,1:41:59.79,1:42:02.24,Default,,0,0,0,,She left in a yellow cab\Nabout a half hour ago.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:02.29,1:42:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't understand.\NWhat? A cab?
Dialogue: 0,1:42:05.06,1:42:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,She said there wasn't no\Nreason for her to stay now\Nthat Mrs. Otis had died.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:09.40,1:42:12.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs...
Dialogue: 0,1:42:12.10,1:42:14.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Otis is dead?
Dialogue: 0,1:42:14.34,1:42:18.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, Mrs. Otis died.
Dialogue: 0,1:42:18.27,1:42:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Otis died!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:20.34,1:42:23.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Otis!\NOh, God!
Dialogue: 0,1:42:23.61,1:42:27.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Not that... I'm glad that\NMrs. Otis died, it's just-
Dialogue: 0,1:42:27.72,1:42:30.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, God.\NI've gotta stop her.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:09.79,1:43:13.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Evelyn,\Nsomebody stole my house.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:13.10,1:43:16.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It was right here\Nwhen I left.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:16.06,1:43:20.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless- Oh, Evelyn,\Nyou don't reckon\NI'm crazy, do you?
Dialogue: 0,1:43:20.90,1:43:25.11,Default,,0,0,0,,- It was here\Nwhen I left.\N- No, honey,\Nyou're not crazy.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:25.17,1:43:27.95,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the place.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:28.01,1:43:32.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would anyone want to\Nsteal an old lady's home?
Dialogue: 0,1:43:32.11,1:43:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Wasn't worth nothin'.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:34.32,1:43:37.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, honey,\Nnobody stole it.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:37.79,1:43:41.67,Default,,0,0,0,,They had to tear it down.\NIt was condemned.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:41.72,1:43:43.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.\NI shoulda told you.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:43.93,1:43:47.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, somebody\Nshoulda told me.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:47.26,1:43:52.11,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'm old.\NI'm not a child.\N- I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:52.17,1:43:55.52,Default,,0,0,0,,My husband Cleo and I\Nlived in this house...
Dialogue: 0,1:43:55.57,1:43:58.07,Default,,0,0,0,,for more than 40 years.
Dialogue: 0,1:43:58.14,1:44:01.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, it's... it's gone.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:01.61,1:44:05.18,Default,,0,0,0,,83 years worth of livin'\Nand all that's left of me...
Dialogue: 0,1:44:05.25,1:44:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,is what's in this box, a\Nbunch of old cards and pictures.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:09.35,1:44:11.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.\NI'll take you home.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:11.89,1:44:14.03,Default,,0,0,0,,This is my home!
Dialogue: 0,1:44:14.09,1:44:16.09,Default,,0,0,0,,And now it's gone.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:16.16,1:44:18.70,Default,,0,0,0,,And Mrs. Otis\Nis gone.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:18.76,1:44:20.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,1:44:20.93,1:44:23.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't quite\Nknow what to do.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:23.60,1:44:27.45,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the first time\NI can remember when I don't\Nhave a soul to look after.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:27.50,1:44:29.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You can come\Nlook after me and Ed.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:29.94,1:44:32.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you're sweet,
Dialogue: 0,1:44:32.31,1:44:35.12,Default,,0,0,0,,but I think you're doin'\Njust fine on your own.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:35.18,1:44:39.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you know you'd be\Nlike a gift for us?
Dialogue: 0,1:44:39.55,1:44:42.72,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the reason\NI get up every morning...
Dialogue: 0,1:44:42.78,1:44:46.13,Default,,0,0,0,,and that Mary Kay's\Nhavin' such a good year...
Dialogue: 0,1:44:46.19,1:44:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,and I don't look like some\Nblob from a horror movie.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:50.83,1:44:54.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,with a little help\Nfrom Idgie and Ruth.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:56.43,1:44:58.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on. I've got\Nyour room all ready.
Dialogue: 0,1:44:59.03,1:45:01.44,Default,,0,0,0,,What does Ed say\Nabout all this?
Dialogue: 0,1:45:01.50,1:45:05.35,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll learn\Nto love it.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:08.81,1:45:12.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I ever tell you\Nthat Mrs. Otis was\NSipsey's baby sister?
Dialogue: 0,1:45:13.01,1:45:15.68,Default,,0,0,0,,- No, ma'am.\N- Yes, she was.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:15.75,1:45:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Otis was with\NSipsey and me the\Nnight Sipsey died.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:44.69,1:45:48.23,Default,,0,0,0,,- Hey there!\N- You got to come quick.
Dialogue: 0,1:45:48.30,1:45:53.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- The show has hardly begun.\N- You got to come quick.\NYou hear me?
Dialogue: 0,1:45:59.17,1:46:01.78,Default,,0,0,0,,- Run, get help!\NRun, quick!\N- Where's the baby?
Dialogue: 0,1:46:01.84,1:46:03.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:22.36,1:46:24.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:24.10,1:46:29.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't believe you\Nshould be goin' anywhere\Nwith Ruth's baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:41.25,1:46:43.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Like I said,\Nyou ain't goin' nowhere.
Dialogue: 0,1:46:44.05,1:46:46.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn, you a thickheaded\Nson-of-a-bitch, ain't you?
Dialogue: 0,1:46:50.83,1:46:52.81,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you...
Dialogue: 0,1:46:52.86,1:46:57.31,Default,,0,0,0,,you ain't goin' nowheres\Nwith Miss Ruth's baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:02.94,1:47:05.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, angel.\NCome on.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:05.21,1:47:09.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, sweetheart.\NIt's all right.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:09.11,1:47:11.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on.\NIt's all right, baby.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:14.52,1:47:17.26,Default,,0,0,0,,it was self-defense.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:17.32,1:47:22.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know why any\Nwhite jury would care\Nwhy I did it.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:22.22,1:47:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,- Well, I saw it,\Nand I can testify.\N- Excuse me here.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:25.09,1:47:27.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't mean\Nno offense here,
Dialogue: 0,1:47:27.33,1:47:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,but I don't know who's less\Nlikely to convince a jury,
Dialogue: 0,1:47:30.46,1:47:32.74,Default,,0,0,0,,my mama...\Nor Mr. Smokey.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:32.80,1:47:35.61,Default,,0,0,0,,No offense taken.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:35.67,1:47:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,You're a good man,\NMr. Smokey.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:38.14,1:47:42.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- You did good.\N- The sun's almost up.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:45.71,1:47:49.09,Default,,0,0,0,,- George?\N- Mm-hmm?
Dialogue: 0,1:47:49.15,1:47:51.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I think...
Dialogue: 0,1:47:51.99,1:47:55.53,Default,,0,0,0,,it's hog-boiling time.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:55.59,1:47:57.87,Default,,0,0,0,,No, ma'am. It\Nain't cold enough.
Dialogue: 0,1:47:57.93,1:48:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It's hog-boiling time.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:03.63,1:48:05.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Big George?
Dialogue: 0,1:48:05.63,1:48:08.74,Default,,0,0,0,,- Uh-huh?\N- When is that barbecue\Ngonna be ready?
Dialogue: 0,1:48:08.80,1:48:11.14,Default,,0,0,0,,It's gonna be ready\Nany time now.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:11.21,1:48:16.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Smells so damn good I just\Ncan't wait to get me some.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:16.18,1:48:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,- Now, don't you forget\Nto call me when that's ready.\N- All right.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:34.23,1:48:36.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Here you go.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:38.07,1:48:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,- Miss Idgie?\NSmokey left town.\N- Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,1:48:41.77,1:48:45.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought it'd be best\Nunder the circumstances.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:45.84,1:48:49.81,Default,,0,0,0,,He asked that\Nyou tell Ruth good-bye.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:49.88,1:48:52.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Shame he had to go.
Dialogue: 0,1:48:59.32,1:49:04.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on! I'm comin'.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:09.10,1:49:11.88,Default,,0,0,0,,- What you want?\N- We want some barbecue.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:11.93,1:49:15.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Not today you don't.\NGo on.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:28.68,1:49:31.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, this is about the\Nbest barbecue I ever ate!
Dialogue: 0,1:49:33.32,1:49:36.82,Default,,0,0,0,,The secret's\Nin the sauce.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:48.05,1:49:51.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel better 'cause\Nall these people'll live...
Dialogue: 0,1:49:51.42,1:49:54.49,Default,,0,0,0,,as long as\Nyou remember 'em.
Dialogue: 0,1:49:54.56,1:49:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,You reminded me...
Dialogue: 0,1:49:56.56,1:49:59.97,Default,,0,0,0,,about what the most\Nimportant thing in life is.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:00.03,1:50:02.37,Default,,0,0,0,,- Do you know\Nwhat I think it is?\N- No, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:02.43,1:50:05.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Friends.\NBest friends.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:05.77,1:50:08.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh. Ninny!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:09.97,1:50:11.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Look.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:16.98,1:50:18.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:38.03,1:50:39.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Idgie?
Dialogue: 0,1:50:43.44,1:50:47.32,Default,,0,0,0,,- Idgie's alive?\N- Oh, yes!
Dialogue: 0,1:50:47.38,1:50:51.66,Default,,0,0,0,,She's still out and about\NCharmin' bees and selling honey.
Dialogue: 0,1:50:51.71,1:50:55.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Sometimes I think\NI catch a glimpse of her.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:01.59,1:51:04.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe we'll\Nsee her today.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:04.09,1:51:06.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:08.40,1:51:11.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:22.61,1:51:26.92,Default,,0,0,0,,After Ruth died and\Nthe railroad stopped runnin',
Dialogue: 0,1:51:26.98,1:51:30.99,Default,,0,0,0,,the cafe shut down, and everybody\Njust scattered to the winds.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:32.32,1:51:35.70,Default,,0,0,0,,It was never more than just\Na little knockabout place.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:35.76,1:51:38.57,Default,,0,0,0,,But now that\NI look back on it,
Dialogue: 0,1:51:38.63,1:51:40.91,Default,,0,0,0,,when that cafe closed...
Dialogue: 0,1:51:40.96,1:51:45.07,Default,,0,0,0,,the heart of the town\Njust stopped beating.
Dialogue: 0,1:51:45.13,1:51:47.97,Default,,0,0,0,,It's funny how\Na little place like this...
Dialogue: 0,1:51:48.04,1:51:51.89,Default,,0,0,0,,brought so
